</div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwBIw" aria-labelledby="Urban_structure"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Urban_structure">Urban structure</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt598" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBI0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Suburbs of Canberra"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt599" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt598" id="mwBI4">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suburbs_of_Canberra" title="Suburbs of Canberra">Suburbs of Canberra</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBI8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Inner-canberra_01MJC.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBJA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Inner-canberra_01MJC.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Inner-canberra_01MJC.png/250px-Inner-canberra_01MJC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Inner-canberra_01MJC.png/500px-Inner-canberra_01MJC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1100" data-file-height="1200" data-file-type="bitmap" height="273" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBJE"/></a><figcaption id="mwBJI">Inner Canberra demonstrates some aspects of the Griffin plan, in particular the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliamentary_Triangle,_Canberra" title="Parliamentary Triangle, Canberra" id="mwBJM">Parliamentary Triangle</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBJQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Civic_Centre-1.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBJU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Civic_Centre-1.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Canberra_Civic_Centre-1.jpg/250px-Canberra_Civic_Centre-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Canberra_Civic_Centre-1.jpg/500px-Canberra_Civic_Centre-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2712" data-file-height="1699" data-file-type="bitmap" height="157" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBJY"/></a><figcaption id="mwBJc">An aerial view of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Civic, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBJg">Civic Centre</a> from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Ainslie" title="Mount Ainslie" id="mwBJk">Mount Ainslie</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBJo">Unusual among Australian cities, Canberra is an entirely <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planned_community" title="Planned community" id="mwBJs">planned city</a>, grounded in a design by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mwBJw">American</a> architects <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Burley_Griffin" title="Walter Burley Griffin" id="mwBJ0">Walter Burley Griffin</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marion_Mahony_Griffin" title="Marion Mahony Griffin" id="mwBJ4">Marion Mahony Griffin</a>.<sup about="#mwt614" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-160" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-160"}}'><a href="#cite_note-160" id="mwBJ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKE">[</span>160<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt617" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-161" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-161"}}'><a href="#cite_note-161" id="mwBKM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKU">[</span>161<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt600" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197160–63_162-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197160–63"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197160–63-162"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"pp":{"wt":"60-63"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197160–63-162" id="mwBKc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKk">[</span>162<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKo">]</span></span></a></sup> Within the central area of the city near Lake Burley Griffin, major roads follow a wheel-and-spoke pattern rather than a grid.<sup about="#mwt603" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197167_163-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197167"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197167-163"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"67"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197167-163" id="mwBKs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBK0">[</span>163<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBK4">]</span></span></a></sup> Griffin's proposal had an abundance of geometric patterns, including concentric hexagonal and octagonal streets emanating from several radii.<sup about="#mwt606" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197167_163-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197167"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197167-163"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"67"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197167-163" id="mwBK8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLE">[</span>163<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLI">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the outer areas of the city, built later, are not laid out geometrically.<sup about="#mwt609" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUniversal_Publishers200710–120_164-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEUniversal Publishers200710–120"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUniversal_Publishers200710–120-164"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Universal Publishers"},"2":{"wt":"2007"},"pp":{"wt":"10-120"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUniversal_Publishers200710–120-164" id="mwBLM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLU">[</span>164<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBLc">Lake Burley Griffin was deliberately designed so that the orientation of the components was related to various topographical landmarks in Canberra.<sup about="#mwt618" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission19883_165-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission19883"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission19883-165"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"3"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission19883-165" id="mwBLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLo">[</span>165<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt621" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164_166-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197164"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"64"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166" id="mwBLw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBL0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL4">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL8">]</span></span></a></sup> The lakes stretch from east to west and divided the city in two; a land axis perpendicular to the central basin stretches from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_Hill,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Capital Hill, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBMA">Capital Hill</a>—the eventual location of the new <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliament_House,_Canberra" title="Parliament House, Canberra" id="mwBME">Parliament House</a> on a mound on the southern side—north northeast across the central basin to the northern banks along <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anzac_Parade,_Canberra" title="Anzac Parade, Canberra" id="mwBMI">Anzac Parade</a> to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_War_Memorial" title="Australian War Memorial" id="mwBMM">Australian War Memorial</a>.<sup about="#mwt624" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke19881–3_95-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke19881–3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke19881–3-95"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"pp":{"wt":"1-3"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke19881–3-95" id="mwBMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMY">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMc">]</span></span></a></sup> This was designed so that looking from Capital Hill, the War Memorial stood directly at the foot of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Ainslie" title="Mount Ainslie" id="mwBMg">Mount Ainslie</a>. At the southwestern end of the land axis was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bimberi_Peak" title="Bimberi Peak" id="mwBMk">Bimberi Peak</a>,<sup about="#mwt627" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164_166-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197164"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"64"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166" id="mwBMo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMw">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBM0">]</span></span></a></sup> the highest mountain in the ACT, approximately <span about="#mwt630" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBM4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"52"},"2":{"wt":"km"},"3":{"wt":"0"}},"i":0}}]}'>52</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt630"> </span><span about="#mwt630">km (32</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt630"> </span><span about="#mwt630">mi)</span> south west of Canberra.<sup about="#mwt631" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200028_138-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPenguin Books Australia200028"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200028-138"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Penguin Books Australia"},"2":{"wt":"2000"},"p":{"wt":"28"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200028-138" id="mwBM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNE">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBNM">The straight edge of the circular segment that formed the central basin of Lake Burley Griffin was perpendicular to the land axis and designated the water axis, and it extended northwest towards <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Mountain_(Australian_Capital_Territory)" title="Black Mountain (Australian Capital Territory)" id="mwBNQ">Black Mountain</a>.<sup about="#mwt634" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164_166-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197164"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"64"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166" id="mwBNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNc">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNg">]</span></span></a></sup> A line parallel to the water axis, on the northern side of the city, was designated the municipal axis.<sup about="#mwt637" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817_167-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission198817"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"17"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167" id="mwBNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNs">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNw">]</span></span></a></sup> The municipal axis became the location of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_Avenue,_Canberra" title="Constitution Avenue, Canberra" id="mwBN0">Constitution Avenue</a>, which links <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Hill,_Canberra" title="City Hill, Canberra" id="mwBN4">City Hill</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="City, Australian Capital Territory" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBN8">Civic Centre</a> and both Market Centre and the Defence precinct on Russell Hill. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Avenue,_Canberra" title="Commonwealth Avenue, Canberra" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBOA">Commonwealth Avenue</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kings_Avenue,_Canberra" title="Kings Avenue, Canberra" id="mwBOE">Kings Avenue</a> were to run from the southern side from Capital Hill to City Hill and Market Centre on the north respectively, and they formed the western and eastern edges of the central basin. The area enclosed by the three avenues was known as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliamentary_Triangle" title="Parliamentary Triangle" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBOI">Parliamentary Triangle</a>, and formed the centrepiece of Griffin's work.<sup about="#mwt640" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164_166-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197164"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"64"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166" id="mwBOM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOU">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt643" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817_167-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission198817"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"17"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167" id="mwBOc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOk">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBOs"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_National_Arboretum_with_Telstra_Tower,_Canberra_ACT.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBOw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_National_Arboretum_with_Telstra_Tower,_Canberra_ACT.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Canberra_National_Arboretum_with_Telstra_Tower%2C_Canberra_ACT.JPG/250px-Canberra_National_Arboretum_with_Telstra_Tower%2C_Canberra_ACT.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Canberra_National_Arboretum_with_Telstra_Tower%2C_Canberra_ACT.JPG/500px-Canberra_National_Arboretum_with_Telstra_Tower%2C_Canberra_ACT.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5184" data-file-height="2948" data-file-type="bitmap" height="142" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBO0"/></a><figcaption id="mwBO4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Mountain_(Australian_Capital_Territory)" title="Black Mountain (Australian Capital Territory)" id="mwBO8">Black Mountain</a> with the landmark <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telstra_Tower" title="Telstra Tower" id="mwBPA">Telstra Tower</a> on the right and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Arboretum_Canberra" title="National Arboretum Canberra" id="mwBPE">National Arboretum</a> in the foreground</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBPI">The Griffins assigned spiritual values to Mount Ainslie, Black Mountain, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Hill,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Red Hill, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBPM">Red Hill</a> and originally planned to cover each of these in flowers. That way each hill would be covered with a single, primary colour which represented its spiritual value.<sup about="#mwt646" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164–67_168-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197164–67"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164–67-168"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"pp":{"wt":"64-67"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164–67-168" id="mwBPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBPU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPY">[</span>168<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPc">]</span></span></a></sup> This part of their plan never came to fruition, as World War I slowed construction and planning disputes led to Griffin's dismissal by Prime Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billy_Hughes" title="Billy Hughes" id="mwBPg">Billy Hughes</a> after the war ended.<sup about="#mwt649" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission19884_77-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission19884"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission19884-77"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"4"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission19884-77" id="mwBPk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBPo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPs">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt652" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197169–79_78-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197169–79"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197169–79-78"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"pp":{"wt":"69-79"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197169–79-78" id="mwBP0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBP4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP8">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt657" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-169" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-169"}}'><a href="#cite_note-169" id="mwBQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQM">[</span>169<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBQU">The urban areas of Canberra are organised into a hierarchy of districts, town centres, group centres, local suburbs as well as other industrial areas and villages. There are seven residential districts, each of which is divided into smaller suburbs, and most of which have a town centre which is the focus of commercial and social activities.<sup about="#mwt658" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUniversal_Publishers200710–60_170-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEUniversal Publishers200710–60"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUniversal_Publishers200710–60-170"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Universal Publishers"},"2":{"wt":"2007"},"pp":{"wt":"10-60"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUniversal_Publishers200710–60-170" id="mwBQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQg">[</span>170<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQk">]</span></span></a></sup> The districts were settled in the following chronological order:</p>
<ul id="mwBQo"><li id="mwBQs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Central" title="Canberra Central" id="mwBQw">Canberra Central</a>, mostly settled in the 1920s and 1930s, with expansion up to the 1960s.<sup about="#mwt661" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGibbney1988110–200_171-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGibbney1988110–200"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGibbney1988110–200-171"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Gibbney"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"pp":{"wt":"110-200"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGibbney1988110–200-171" id="mwBQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQ8">[</span>171<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBRE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woden_Valley" title="Woden Valley" id="mwBRI">Woden Valley</a>, first settled in 1964.<sup about="#mwt664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988180_109-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988180"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988180-109"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"180"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988180-109" id="mwBRM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRU">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBRc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belconnen" title="Belconnen" id="mwBRg">Belconnen</a>, first settled in 1966.<sup about="#mwt667" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988180_109-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988180"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988180-109"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"180"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988180-109" id="mwBRk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRs">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBR0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weston_Creek" title="Weston Creek" id="mwBR4">Weston Creek</a>, first settled in 1969.<sup about="#mwt672" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-172" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-172" id="mwBR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSE">[</span>172<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBSM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuggeranong" title="Tuggeranong" id="mwBSQ">Tuggeranong</a>, first settled in 1974.<sup about="#mwt673" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFitzgerald1987167_173-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEFitzgerald1987167"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFitzgerald1987167-173"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Fitzgerald"},"2":{"wt":"1987"},"p":{"wt":"167"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFitzgerald1987167-173" id="mwBSU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSc">[</span>173<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBSk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gungahlin" title="Gungahlin" id="mwBSo">Gungahlin</a>, first settled in 1991.<sup about="#mwt678" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-174" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-174"}}'><a href="#cite_note-174" id="mwBSs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBS0">[</span>174<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBS4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBS8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molonglo_Valley" title="Molonglo Valley" id="mwBTA">Molonglo Valley</a>, development began in 2010.<sup about="#mwt681" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-175" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-175"}}'><a href="#cite_note-175" id="mwBTE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTM">[</span>175<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwBTU">The Canberra Central district is substantially based on Walter Burley Griffin's designs.<sup about="#mwt682" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164_166-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197164"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"64"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197164-166" id="mwBTY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTg">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt685" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817_167-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission198817"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"17"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167" id="mwBTo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTw">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt694" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-map_176-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"map"}}'><a href="#cite_note-map-176" id="mwBT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUA">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUE">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1967 the then <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Capital_Development_Commission" title="National Capital Development Commission" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBUI">National Capital Development Commission</a> adopted the "Y Plan" which laid out future urban development in Canberra around a series of central shopping and commercial area known as the 'town centres' linked by freeways, the layout of which roughly resembled the shape of the letter Y,<sup about="#mwt688" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155_177-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155-177"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"pp":{"wt":"154-155"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155-177" id="mwBUM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUU">[</span>177<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUY">]</span></span></a></sup> with Tuggeranong at the base of the Y and Belconnen and Gungahlin located at the ends of the arms of the Y.<sup about="#mwt691" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155_177-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155-177"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"pp":{"wt":"154-155"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988154–155-177" id="mwBUc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUk">[</span>177<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBUs">Development in Canberra has been closely regulated by government,<sup about="#mwt697" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-178" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-178"}}'><a href="#cite_note-178" id="mwBUw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBU0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBU4">[</span>178<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBU8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt700" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rest_179-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rest"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-rest-179"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rest-179" id="mwBVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVI">[</span>179<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVM">]</span></span></a></sup> both through planning processes and the use of crown lease terms that have tightly limited the use of parcels of land. Land in the ACT is held on 99-year crown leases from the national government, although most leases are now administered by the Territory government.<sup about="#mwt703" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-180" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-180"}}'><a href="#cite_note-180" id="mwBVQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVY">[</span>180<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVc">]</span></span></a></sup> There have been persistent calls for constraints on development to be liberalised,<sup about="#mwt704" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rest_179-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rest"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rest-179" id="mwBVg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVo">[</span>179<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVs">]</span></span></a></sup> but also voices in support of planning consistent with the original 'bush capital' and 'urban forest' ideals that underpin Canberra's design.<sup about="#mwt707" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-181" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-181"}}'><a href="#cite_note-181" id="mwBVw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBV0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBV4">[</span>181<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBV8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBWA">Many of Canberra's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Canberra_suburbs" title="List of Canberra suburbs" id="mwBWE">suburbs</a> are named after former Prime Ministers, famous Australians, early settlers, or use Aboriginal words for their title.<sup about="#mwt708" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-name_182-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"name"}}'><a href="#cite_note-name-182" id="mwBWI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWQ">[</span>182<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWU">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_name" title="Street name" id="mwBWY">Street names</a> typically follow a particular theme; for example, the streets of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duffy,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Duffy, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBWc">Duffy</a> are named after Australian dams and reservoirs, the streets of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunlop,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Dunlop, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBWg">Dunlop</a> are named after Australian inventions, inventors and artists and the streets of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Page,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Page, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBWk">Page</a> are named after biologists and naturalists.<sup about="#mwt711" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-name_182-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"name"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-name-182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-name-182" id="mwBWo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWw">[</span>182<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBW0">]</span></span></a></sup> Most <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_mission" title="Diplomatic mission" id="mwBW4">diplomatic missions</a> are located in the suburbs of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yarralumla,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Yarralumla, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBW8">Yarralumla</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deakin,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Deakin, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBXA">Deakin</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/O'Malley,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="O'Malley, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBXE">O'Malley</a>.<sup about="#mwt714" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-183" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-183"}}'><a href="#cite_note-183" id="mwBXI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXQ">[</span>183<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXU">]</span></span></a></sup> There are three light industrial areas: the suburbs of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyshwick,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Fyshwick, Australian Capital Territory" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBXY">Fyshwick</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitchell,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Mitchell, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBXc">Mitchell</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hume,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Hume, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBXg">Hume</a>.<sup about="#mwt717" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-184" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-184"}}'><a href="#cite_note-184" id="mwBXk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXs">[</span>184<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt718" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBX0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"wide image","href":"./Template:Wide_image"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Canberra From Black Mountain Tower.jpg"},"2":{"wt":"800px"},"3":{"wt":"Panorama of Canberra and Lake Burley Griffin set against the backdrop of distant New South Wales, taken from the [[Telstra Tower]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1330227556" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt719" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Wide image/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .wide-image-normbg,.mw-parser-output .thumbimage.wide-image-normbg{background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle,#f8f9fa);color:inherit}.mw-parser-output .wide-image-nobg,.mw-parser-output .thumbimage.wide-image-nobg{background:transparent;color:inherit}</style></span><div class="thumb tnone" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;overflow:hidden;width:auto;max-width:810px" about="#mwt718" id="mwBX4"><div class="thumbinner"><div class="noresize thumbimage" style="overflow:auto"><span typeof="mw:File" data-mw='{"caption":"Panorama of Canberra and Lake Burley Griffin set against the backdrop of distant New South Wales, taken from the &lt;a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"./Telstra_Tower\" title=\"Telstra Tower\" id=\"mwBX8\">Telstra Tower&lt;/a>"}'><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_From_Black_Mountain_Tower.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Panorama of Canberra and Lake Burley Griffin set against the backdrop of distant New South Wales, taken from the Telstra Tower"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_From_Black_Mountain_Tower.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Canberra_From_Black_Mountain_Tower.jpg/960px-Canberra_From_Black_Mountain_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb