tr></tbody></table></td><td style="width:0.2%;vertical-align:top"><table style="width:100%;font-size:85%;line-height:95%"><tbody><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:blue"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Burley_Griffin" title="Lake Burley Griffin"><span title="Lake Burley Griffin" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">13</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Burley_Griffin" title="Lake Burley Griffin">Lake Burley Griffin</a></td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limestone_Avenue,_Canberra" title="Limestone Avenue, Canberra" class="mw-redirect"><span title="Limestone Avenue" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">14</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limestone_Avenue,_Canberra" title="Limestone Avenue, Canberra" class="mw-redirect">Limestone Avenue</a></td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairbairn_Avenue" title="Fairbairn Avenue"><span title="Fairbairn Avenue" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">15</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairbairn_Avenue" title="Fairbairn Avenue">Fairbairn Avenue</a></td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkes_Way" title="Parkes Way"><span title="Parkes Way" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">16</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkes_Way" title="Parkes Way">Parkes Way</a></td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Foreign_Affairs_and_Trade_(Australia)" title="Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (Australia)"><span title="R G Casey Building" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">17</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Foreign_Affairs_and_Trade_(Australia)" title="Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (Australia)">R G Casey Building</a></td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Gorton_Building" title="John Gorton Building"><span title="John Gorton Building" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">18</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Gorton_Building" title="John Gorton Building">John Gorton Building</a></td></tr></tbody></table></td><td style="width:0.2%;vertical-align:top"><table style="width:100%;font-size:85%;line-height:95%"><tbody><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><span title="King Edward Terrace" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">19</span></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px">King Edward Terrace</td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><span title="Presbyterian Church of Saint Andrew" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">20</span></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px">Presbyterian Church of Saint Andrew</td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top"><td style="width:12px;text-align:right;padding-bottom:2px"><div style="display:inline-block;width:auto;height:auto;text-align:center;padding:0px 2px;vertical-align:middle;border-radius:3px;background-color:red"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_John_the_Baptist_Church,_Reid" title="St John the Baptist Church, Reid"><span title="St John's Anglican Church" style="color:white;font-size:88%;font-weight:bold">21</span></a></div></td><td style="padding-bottom:2px"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_John_the_Baptist_Church,_Reid" title="St John the Baptist Church, Reid">St John's Anglican Church</a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwBYE" aria-labelledby="Sustainability_and_the_environment"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Sustainability_and_the_environment">Sustainability and the environment</h3></div>
<p id="mwBYI">The average Canberran was responsible for 13.7 tonnes of greenhouse gases in 2005.<sup about="#mwt723" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-185" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-185"}}'><a href="#cite_note-185" id="mwBYM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYU">[</span>185<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYY">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2012, the ACT Government legislated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenhouse_gas" title="Greenhouse gas" id="mwBYc">greenhouse gas</a> targets to reduce its emissions by 40<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBYg"> </span>per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBYk"> </span>cent from 1990 levels by 2020, 80<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBYo"> </span>per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBYs"> </span>cent by 2050, with no net emissions by<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBYw"> </span>2060.<sup about="#mwt726" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-186" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-186"}}'><a href="#cite_note-186" id="mwBY0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBY4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBY8">[</span>186<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZA">]</span></span></a></sup> The government announced in 2013 a target for 90% of electricity consumed in the ACT to be supplied from renewable sources by 2020,<sup about="#mwt727" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-renewable_187-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"renewable"}}'><a href="#cite_note-renewable-187" id="mwBZE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZM">[</span>187<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and in 2016 set an ambitious target of 100% by 2020.<sup about="#mwt730" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-188" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-188"}}'><a href="#cite_note-188" id="mwBZU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZc">[</span>188<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt733" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-189" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-189"}}'><a href="#cite_note-189" id="mwBZk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZs">[</span>189<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZw">]</span></span></a></sup> Canberra achieved 100% renewable electricity in 2020 and the ACT Government committed in 2024 to Canberra using 100% renewable energy in 2045.<sup about="#mwt736" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-190" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-190"}}'><a href="#cite_note-190" id="mwBZ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZ8">[</span>190<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBaE">In 1996, Canberra became the first city in the world to set a vision of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zero_waste" title="Zero waste" id="mwBaI">no waste</a>, proposing an ambitious target of 2010 for completion.<sup about="#mwt739" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-191" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-191"}}'><a href="#cite_note-191" id="mwBaM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaU">[</span>191<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaY">]</span></span></a></sup> The strategy aimed to achieve a waste-free society by 2010, through the combined efforts of industry, government and community.<sup about="#mwt742" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-192" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-192"}}'><a href="#cite_note-192" id="mwBac"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBak">[</span>192<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBao">]</span></span></a></sup> By early 2010, it was apparent that though it had reduced waste going to landfill, the ACT initiative's original 2010 target for absolutely zero landfill waste would be delayed or revised to meet the reality.<sup about="#mwt745" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-193" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-193"}}'><a href="#cite_note-193" id="mwBas"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBaw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBa0">[</span>193<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBa4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt748" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-194" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-194"}}'><a href="#cite_note-194" id="mwBa8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbE">[</span>194<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBbM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic_bags" title="Plastic bags" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBbQ">Plastic bags</a> made of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyethylene" title="Polyethylene" id="mwBbU">polyethylene</a> polymer with a thickness of less than 35<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBbY"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Μm" title="Μm" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBbc">μm</a> were banned from retail distribution in the ACT from November 2011.<sup about="#mwt752" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-195" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-195"}}'><a href="#cite_note-195" id="mwBbg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbo">[</span>195<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt755" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PlasticBags_196-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"PlasticBags"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-PlasticBags-196"}}'><a href="#cite_note-PlasticBags-196" id="mwBbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBb0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBb4">[</span>196<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBb8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt758" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-197" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-197"}}'><a href="#cite_note-197" id="mwBcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcI">[</span>197<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcM">]</span></span></a></sup> The ban was introduced by the ACT Government in an effort to make Canberra more sustainable.<sup about="#mwt759" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PlasticBags_196-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"PlasticBags"}}'><a href="#cite_note-PlasticBags-196" id="mwBcQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcY">[</span>196<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBcg">Of all waste produced in the ACT, 75<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBck"> </span>per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBco"> </span>cent is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recycled" title="Recycled" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBcs">recycled</a>.<sup about="#mwt762" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-198" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-198"}}'><a href="#cite_note-198" id="mwBcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBc0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc4">[</span>198<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBc8">]</span></span></a></sup> Average household <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_waste" title="Food waste" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBdA">food waste</a> in the ACT remains above the Australian average, costing an average $641<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBdE"> </span>per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBdI"> </span>household per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBdM"> </span>annum.<sup about="#mwt765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-199" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-199"}}'><a href="#cite_note-199" id="mwBdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdY">[</span>199<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwBdg" aria-labelledby="Government_and_politics"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Government_and_politics">Government and politics</h2></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwBdk" aria-labelledby="Territory_government"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Territory_government">Territory government</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt766" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBdo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Australian Capital Territory Legislative Assembly"},"2":{"wt":"Electoral systems of the Australian states and territories"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt767" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt766" id="mwBds">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Capital_Territory_Legislative_Assembly" title="Australian Capital Territory Legislative Assembly">Australian Capital Territory Legislative Assembly</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_systems_of_the_Australian_states_and_territories" title="Electoral systems of the Australian states and territories">Electoral systems of the Australian states and territories</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBdw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_to_the_ACT_Legislative_Assembly_building_July_2022.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBd0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_to_the_ACT_Legislative_Assembly_building_July_2022.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Entrance_to_the_ACT_Legislative_Assembly_building_July_2022.jpg/250px-Entrance_to_the_ACT_Legislative_Assembly_building_July_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Entrance_to_the_ACT_Legislative_Assembly_building_July_2022.jpg/500px-Entrance_to_the_ACT_Legislative_Assembly_building_July_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBd4"/></a><figcaption id="mwBd8">ACT Legislative Assembly<br id="mwBeA"/>and the statue <i id="mwBeE">Ethos</i> (Tom Bass, 1961)</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBeI">There is no local council or city government for Canberra, which thus has no precise definition. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Capital_Territory_Legislative_Assembly" title="Australian Capital Territory Legislative Assembly" id="mwBeM">Australian Capital Territory Legislative Assembly</a> administers both the urban area and the rest of the Australian Capital Territory.<sup about="#mwt768" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ass_116-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ass"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ass-116" id="mwBeQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeY">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBec">]</span></span></a></sup> At the 2021 census, all but 888 people were calculated to reside in the urban area of Canberra.<sup about="#mwt769" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_200-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-200" id="mwBeg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBek"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeo">[</span>200<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBes">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt770" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2021_201-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2021-201" id="mwBew"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBe0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe4">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBe8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBfA">The assembly consists of 25 members elected from five districts using proportional representation. The five districts are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brindabella_electorate" title="Brindabella electorate" id="mwBfE">Brindabella</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginninderra_electorate" title="Ginninderra electorate" id="mwBfI">Ginninderra</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurrajong_electorate" title="Kurrajong electorate" id="mwBfM">Kurrajong</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murrumbidgee_electorate" title="Murrumbidgee electorate" id="mwBfQ">Murrumbidgee</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yerrabi_electorate" title="Yerrabi electorate" id="mwBfU">Yerrabi</a>, which each elect five members.<sup about="#mwt773" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-elecpage_202-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"elecpage"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-elecpage-202"}}'><a href="#cite_note-elecpage-202" id="mwBfY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfg">[</span>202<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfk">]</span></span></a></sup> The Chief Minister is elected by the Members of the Legislative Assembly (MLA) and selects colleagues to serve as ministers alongside him or her in the Executive, known informally as the cabinet.<sup about="#mwt774" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ass_116-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ass"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ass-116" id="mwBfo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfw">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBf0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBf4">Whereas the ACT has federally been dominated by Labor,<sup about="#mwt778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABCelections2007_203-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABCelections2007"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABCelections2007-203" id="mwBf8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgE">[</span>203<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt779" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fras_204-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"fras"}}'><a href="#cite_note-fras-204" id="mwBgM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgU">[</span>204<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgY">]</span></span></a></sup> the Liberals have been able to gain some footing in the ACT Legislative Assembly and were in government during a period of <style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1154941027" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt775" id="mwBgc" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Fraction/styles.css"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"frac","href":"./Template:Frac"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"6"},"2":{"wt":"1"},"3":{"wt":"2"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output .frac{white-space:nowrap}.mw-parser-output .frac .num,.mw-parser-output .frac .den{font-size:80%;line-height:0;vertical-align:super}.mw-parser-output .frac .den{vertical-align:sub}.mw-parser-output .sr-only{border:0;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);clip-path:polygon(0px 0px,0px 0px,0px 0px);height:1px;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;padding:0;position:absolute;width:1px}</style><span class="frac" about="#mwt775" id="mwBgg">6<span class="sr-only">+</span><span class="num">1</span><span typeof="mw:Entity">⁄</span><span class="den">2</span></span> years from 1995 and 2001. Labor took back control of the Assembly in 2001.<sup about="#mwt780" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-state_el_117-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"state_el"}}'><a href="#cite_note-state_el-117" id="mwBgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgs">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgw">]</span></span></a></sup> At the 2004 election, Chief Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Stanhope" title="Jon Stanhope" id="mwBg0">Jon Stanhope</a> and the Labor Party won 9 of the 17 seats allowing them to form the ACT's first majority government.<sup about="#mwt781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-state_el_117-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"state_el"}}'><a href="#cite_note-state_el-117" id="mwBg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhA">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhE">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2008, the ACT has been governed by a coalition of Labor and the Greens.<sup about="#mwt782" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-state_el_117-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"state_el"}}'><a href="#cite_note-state_el-117" id="mwBhI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhQ">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt785" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-anniv_205-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"anniv"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-anniv-205"}}'><a href="#cite_note-anniv-205" id="mwBhY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhg">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt788" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-206" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-206"}}'><a href="#cite_note-206" id="mwBho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhw">[</span>206<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBh0">]</span></span></a></sup> <span about="#mwt777" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBh4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2022"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2022</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt777"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Canberra&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Canberra&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt777"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2022" about="#mwt777"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt777" id="mwBh8"/>, the Chief Minister was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Barr" title="Andrew Barr" id="mwBiA">Andrew Barr</a> from the Australian Labor Party.</p>

<p id="mwBiE">The Australian federal government retains some influence over the ACT government. In the administrative sphere, most frequently this is through the actions of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Capital_Authority" title="National Capital Authority" id="mwBiI">National Capital Authority</a> which is responsible for planning and development in areas of Canberra which are considered to be of national importance or which are central to Griffin's plan for the city,<sup about="#mwt791" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nca_207-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nca"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nca-207"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nca-207" id="mwBiM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiU">[</span>207<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiY">]</span></span></a></sup> such as the Parliamentary Triangle, Lake Burley Griffin, major approach and processional roads, areas where the Commonwealth retains ownership of the land or undeveloped hills and ridge-lines (which form part of the Canberra Nature Park).<sup about="#mwt792" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nca_207-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nca"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nca-207" id="mwBic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBik">[</span>207<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBio">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt795" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-208" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-208"}}'><a href="#cite_note-208" id="mwBis"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBiw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBi0">[</span>208<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBi4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt798" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-209" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-209"}}'><a href="#cite_note-209" id="mwBi8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjE">[</span>209<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjI">]</span></span></a></sup> The national government also retains a level of control over the Territory Assembly through the provisions of the <i id="mwBjM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Capital_Territory_(Self-Government)_Act_1988" title="Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988" id="mwBjQ">Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt800" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-210" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-210"}}'><a href="#cite_note-210" id="mwBjU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjc">[</span>210<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjg">]</span></span></a></sup> This federal act defines the legislative power of the ACT assembly.<sup about="#mwt802" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-211" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-211"}}'><a href="#cite_note-211" id="mwBjk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjs">[</span>211<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwBj0" aria-labelledby="Federal_representation"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Federal_representation">Federal representation</h3></div>
<p id="mwBj4">The ACT was given its first federal parliamentary representation in 1949 when it gained a seat in the House of Representatives, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Division_of_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Division of Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBj8">Division of Australian Capital Territory</a>.<sup about="#mwt803" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988289_212-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988289"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988289-212"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"289"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988289-212" id="mwBkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkI">[</span>212<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt809" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1948act_213-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"1948act"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1948act-213" id="mwBkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkY">[</span>213<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkc">]</span></span></a></sup> However, until 1966, the ACT member could only vote on matters directly affecting the territory and did not count for purposes of forming government.<sup about="#mwt812" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1948act_213-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"1948act"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-1948act-213"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1948act-213" id="mwBkg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBko">[</span>213<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBks">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1974, the ACT was allocated two Senate seats and the House of Representatives seat was divided into two.<sup about="#mwt806" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988289_212-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988289"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988289-212"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"289"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988289-212" id="mwBkw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBk0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBk4">[</span>212<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBk8">]</span></span></a></sup> A third was created in 1996, but was abolished in 1998 because of changes to the regional demographic distribution.<sup about="#mwt813" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABCelections2007_203-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABCelections2007"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABCelections2007-203" id="mwBlA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlI">[</span>203<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlM">]</span></span></a></sup> A third seat was recreated at a redistribution in 2018 as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Division_of_Bean" title="Division of Bean" id="mwBlQ">Division of Bean</a>.<sup about="#mwt816" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-214" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-214"}}'><a href="#cite_note-214" id="mwBlU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlc">[</span>214<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlg">]</span></span></a></sup> The House of Representatives seats have mostly been held by Labor and usually by comfortable margins.<sup about="#mwt819" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABCelections2007_203-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABCelections2007"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABCelections2007-203"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABCelections2007-203" id="mwBlk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBls">[</span>203<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt822" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fras_204-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"fras"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-fras-204"}}'><a href="#cite_note-fras-204" id="mwBl0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBl4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBl8">[</span>204<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmA">]</span></span></a></sup> The Labor Party has held all seats at every federal election since 1980, although it lost a byelection for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Division_of_Canberra" title="Division of Canberra" id="mwBmE">Division of Canberra</a> in 1995.<sup about="#mwt825" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-state_el_117-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"state_el"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-state_el-117"}}'><a href="#cite_note-state_el-117" id="mwBmI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmQ">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmU">]</span></span></a></sup> The ALP and the Liberal Party held one Senate seat each until the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Australian_federal_election" title="2022 Australian federal election" id="mwBmY">2022 election</a> when Independent candidate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Pocock" title="David Pocock" id="mwBmc">David Pocock</a> unseated the Liberal candidate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zed_Seselja" title="Zed Seselja" id="mwBmg">Zed Seselja</a>.<sup about="#mwt828" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-215" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-215"}}'><a href="#cite_note-215" id="mwBmk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBms">[</span>215<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwBm0" aria-labelledby="Judiciary_and_policing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Judiciary_and_policing">Judiciary and policing</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt829" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBm4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Magistrates Court of the Australian Capital Territory"},"2":{"wt":"Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory"},"3":{"wt":"ACT Policing"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt830" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt829" id="mwBm8">Main articles: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magistrates_Court_of_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Magistrates Court of the Australian Capital Territory">Magistrates Court of the Australian Capital Territory</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory">Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACT_Policing" title="ACT Policing">ACT Policing</a></div>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt831" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBnA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Crime in the Australian Capital Territory"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt832" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt831" id="mwBnE">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crime_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Crime in the Australian Capital Territory">Crime in the Australian Capital Territory</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBnI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:High_Court_Canberra_Australia.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBnM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:High_Court_Canberra_Australia.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/High_Court_Canberra_Australia.jpg/250px-High_Court_Canberra_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/High_Court_Canberra_Australia.jpg/500px-High_Court_Canberra_Australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4649" data-file-height="3461" data-file-type="bitmap" height="186" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBnQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwBnU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Court_of_Australia" title="High Court of Australia" id="mwBnY">High Court of Australia</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBnc">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Federal_Police" title="Australian Federal Police" id="mwBng">Australian Federal Police</a> (AFP) provides all of the constabulary services in the territory in a manner similar to state police forces, under a contractual agreement with the ACT Government, through its community policing arm, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACT_Policing" title="ACT Policing" id="mwBnk">ACT Policing</a>.<sup about="#mwt835" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-afpact_216-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"afpact"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-afpact-216"}}'><a href="#cite_note-afpact-216" id="mwBno"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBns"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnw">[</span>216<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn0">]</span></span></a></sup> 
People who have been charged with offences are tried either in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magistrates_Court_of_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Magistrates Court of the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBn4">ACT Magistrates Court</a> or, for more severe offences, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBn8">ACT Supreme Court</a>.<sup about="#mwt838" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-217" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-217" id="mwBoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoI">[</span>217<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoM">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2009, prisoners, including those on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-trial_detention" title="Pre-trial detention" id="mwBoQ">remand</a> have been held at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Maconochie_Centre" title="Alexander Maconochie Centre" id="mwBoU">Alexander Maconochie Centre</a>.<sup about="#mwt841" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-218" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-218"}}'><a href="#cite_note-218" id="mwBoY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBog">[</span>218<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBok">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACT_Civil_and_Administrative_Tribunal" title="ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal" id="mwBoo">ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal</a> deal with minor civil law actions and other various legal matters.<sup about="#mwt844" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-219" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-219"}}'><a href="#cite_note-219" id="mwBos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo0">[</span>219<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBo8">Canberra is often described as Australia's safest city.<sup about="#mwt848" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-220" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-220"}}'><a href="#cite_note-220" id="mwBpA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpI">[</span>220<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpM">]</span></span></a></sup> <span about="#mwt845" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBpQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2024"}},"i":0}}]}'>As of 2024</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt845"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Canberra&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Canberra&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt845"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2024" about="#mwt845"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt845" id="mwBpU"/>, the most common crimes in the ACT were property related crimes, unlawful entry with intent and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motor_vehicle_theft" title="Motor vehicle theft" id="mwBpY">motor vehicle theft</a>. They affected 1,449 and 920 people (305 and 193 per 100,000 persons respectively). Rates of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_assault" title="Sexual assault" id="mwBpc">sexual assault</a>, 428 (89 per 100,000 persons) are also below the national average (147 per 100,000). These rates are lower than the equivalent figures for other states and the Northern Territory, except for motor vehicle theft.<sup about="#mwt851" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-221" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-221"}}'><a href="#cite_note-221" id="mwBpg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpo">[</span>221<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBps">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt854" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-222" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-222"}}'><a href="#cite_note-222" id="mwBpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBp0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp4">[</span>222<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwBqA" aria-labelledby="Economy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Economy">Economy</h2></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBqE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ACT_Government,_Canberra.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBqI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ACT_Government,_Canberra.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/ACT_Government%2C_Canberra.jpg/250px-ACT_Government%2C_Canberra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/ACT_Government%2C_Canberra.jpg/500px-ACT_Government%2C_Canberra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4000" data-file-height="2252" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBqM"/></a><figcaption id="mwBqQ">Just under a third of Canberrans are employed in the public sector, working in government departments such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Government of the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBqU">ACT Government</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBqY">In November 2025, the unemployment rate in Canberra was 4.4%, almost identical with the national unemployment rate of 4.3%.<sup about="#mwt857" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-223" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-223"}}'><a href="#cite_note-223" id="mwBqc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqk">[</span>223<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqo">]</span></span></a></sup> Canberra had a higher median level of weekly personal income than any Australian state capital (which ranged from $762 to $881) at the 2021 census. The median level of personal income was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_dollar" title="Australian dollar" id="mwBqs">$</a>1,204 compared with the national average of $805.<sup about="#mwt860" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8ACTE_2021_224-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"8ACTE 2021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8ACTE_2021-224"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8ACTE_2021-224" id="mwBqw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBq0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq4">[</span>224<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt863" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-225" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-225"}}'><a href="#cite_note-225" id="mwBrA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrI">[</span>225<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt866" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-226" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-226"}}'><a href="#cite_note-226" id="mwBrQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrY">[</span>226<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt869" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-227" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-227"}}'><a href="#cite_note-227" id="mwBrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBro">[</span>227<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt872" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-228" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-228"}}'><a href="#cite_note-228" id="mwBrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr4">[</span>228<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt875" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-229" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-229"}}'><a href="#cite_note-229" id="mwBsA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsI">[</span>229<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt878" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-230" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-230"}}'><a href="#cite_note-230" id="mwBsQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsY">[</span>230<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsc">]</span></span></a></sup> The median house price in Canberra as of December 2025 was $893,907, lower than Sydney, Brisbane, Perth and Adelaide, but higher than Melbourne, Hobart and Darwin, among capital cities.<sup about="#mwt881" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-APU_231-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"APU"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-APU-231"}}'><a href="#cite_note-APU-231" id="mwBsg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBso">[</span>231<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBss">]</span></span></a></sup> Median weekly rents in Canberra in June 2025 of $677 were similarly about midway in comparison with other state and territory capital cities.<sup about="#mwt884" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-232" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-232"}}'><a href="#cite_note-232" id="mwBsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBs0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs4">[</span>232<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBtA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:50_Marcus_Clarke_Street_Feb_2016.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBtE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:50_Marcus_Clarke_Street_Feb_2016.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/50_Marcus_Clarke_Street_Feb_2016.jpg/250px-50_Marcus_Clarke_Street_Feb_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/50_Marcus_Clarke_Street_Feb_2016.jpg/500px-50_Marcus_Clarke_Street_Feb_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBtI"/></a><figcaption id="mwBtM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Civic, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwBtQ">Civic</a> is home to various administrative departments, such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Education,_Skills_and_Employment" title="Department of Education, Skills and Employment" id="mwBtU">Department of Education, Skills and Employment</a></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBtY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bunda_Street_July_2021.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBtc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bunda_Street_July_2021.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Bunda_Street_July_2021.jpg/250px-Bunda_Street_July_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Bunda_Street_July_2021.jpg/500px-Bunda_Street_July_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBtg"/></a><figcaption id="mwBtk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunda_Street" title="Bunda Street" id="mwBto">Bunda Street</a> in Canberra's shopping district; tourism, retail and hospitality are also major employers.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBts">The city's main industry is public administration and safety, which accounted for 27.1% of Gross Territory Product in 2018–19 and employed 32.49% of Canberra's workforce.<sup about="#mwt888" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-233" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-233"}}'><a href="#cite_note-233" id="mwBtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBt0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBt4">[</span>233<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBt8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt891" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EDA_ACT_Economic_Indicators_234-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EDA ACT Economic Indicators"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-EDA_ACT_Economic_Indicators-234"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EDA_ACT_Economic_Indicators-234" id="mwBuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuI">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuM">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Public_Service" title="Australian Public Service" id="mwBuQ">Australian Public Service</a> accounted for about 25% all jobs as at November 2025.<sup about="#mwt894" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-235" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-235"}}'><a href="#cite_note-235" id="mwBuU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuc">[</span>235<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBug">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt897" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-236" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-236"}}'><a href="#cite_note-236" id="mwBuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBus">[</span>236<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuw">]</span></span></a></sup> The headquarters of many Australian Public Service agencies are located in Canberra, and Canberra is also host to several <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Defence_Force" title="Australian Defence Force" id="mwBu0">Australian Defence Force</a> establishments, most notably the Australian Defence Force headquarters and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HMAS_Harman" title="HMAS Harman" about="#mwt885" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBu4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"HMAS","href":"./Template:HMAS"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Harman"}},"i":0}}]}'>HMAS<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><i>Harman</i></a>, which is a naval communications centre that is being converted into a tri-service, multi-user depot.<sup about="#mwt900" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-237" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-237"}}'><a href="#cite_note-237" id="mwBu8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvE">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvI">]</span></span></a></sup> Other major sectors by employment include Health Care (10.54%), Professional Services (9.77%), Education and Training (9.64%), Retail (7.27%), Accommodation &amp; Food (6.39%) and Construction (5.80%).</p>

<p id="mwBvM"><sup about="#mwt901" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EDA_ACT_Economic_Indicators_234-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EDA ACT Economic Indicators"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EDA_ACT_Economic_Indicators-234" id="mwBvQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvY">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvc">]</span></span></a></sup></p><figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBvg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NASA's_Deep_Space_Antenna_Upgrade_to_Affect_Voyager.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBvk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NASA's_Deep_Space_Antenna_Upgrade_to_Affect_Voyager.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/NASA%27s_Deep_Space_Antenna_Upgrade_to_Affect_Voyager.jpg/250px-NASA%27s_Deep_Space_Antenna_Upgrade_to_Affect_Voyager.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/NASA%27s_Deep_Space_Antenna_Upgrade_to_Affect_Voyager.jpg/500px-NASA%27s_Deep_Space_Antenna_Upgrade_to_Affect_Voyager.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1920" data-file-height="1280" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBvo"/></a><figcaption id="mwBvs">A growing number of Canberrans work in the science and technology sector, such as at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Deep_Space_Communication_Complex" title="Canberra Deep Space Communication Complex" id="mwBvw">Canberra Deep Space Communication Complex</a>.</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBv0">The former <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairbairn_Airbase" title="Fairbairn Airbase" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBv4">RAAF Fairbairn</a>, adjacent to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Airport" title="Canberra Airport" id="mwBv8">Canberra Airport</a> was sold to the operators of the airport,<sup about="#mwt904" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fb_238-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"fb"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-fb-238"}}'><a href="#cite_note-fb-238" id="mwBwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwI">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwM">]</span></span></a></sup> but the base continues to be used for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RAAF" title="RAAF" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBwQ">RAAF</a> VIP flights.<sup about="#mwt907" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-239" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-239"}}'><a href="#cite_note-239" id="mwBwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwc">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt910" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-240" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-240"}}'><a href="#cite_note-240" id="mwBwk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBws">[</span>240<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBww">]</span></span></a></sup> A growing number of software vendors have based themselves in Canberra, to capitalise on the concentration of government customers; these include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower_Software" title="Tower Software" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBw0">Tower Software</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RuleBurst" title="RuleBurst" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBw4">RuleBurst</a>.<sup about="#mwt913" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-241" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-241"}}'><a href="#cite_note-241" id="mwBw8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxE">[</span>241<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt916" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-242" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-242"}}'><a href="#cite_note-242" id="mwBxM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxU">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxY">]</span></span></a></sup> A consortium of private and government investors is making plans for a billion-dollar data hub, with the aim of making Canberra a leading centre of such activity in the Asia-Pacific region.<sup about="#mwt919" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-243" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-243"}}'><a href="#cite_note-243" id="mwBxc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxk">[</span>243<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxo">]</span></span></a></sup> A Canberra Cyber Security Innovation Node was established in 2019 to grow the ACT's cyber security sector and related space, defence and education industries.<sup about="#mwt922" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-244" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-244"}}'><a href="#cite_note-244" id="mwBxs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBx0">[</span>244<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBx4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwBx8" aria-labelledby="Demographics"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Demographics">Demographics</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt923" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwByA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Demographics of Canberra"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt924" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt923" id="mwByE">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_Canberra" title="Demographics of Canberra">Demographics of Canberra</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwByI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Belconnen_Apartments_-_DSC07473-HDR.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwByM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Belconnen_Apartments_-_DSC07473-HDR.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Belconnen_Apartments_-_DSC07473-HDR.jpg/250px-Belconnen_Apartments_-_DSC07473-HDR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Belconnen_Apartments_-_DSC07473-HDR.jpg/500px-Belconnen_Apartments_-_DSC07473-HDR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4307" data-file-height="3465" data-file-type="bitmap" height="201" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwByQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwByU">High-density residential apartments in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belconnen" title="Belconnen" id="mwByY">Belconnen</a>; Canberra has one of the fastest growing populations in the nation<sup about="#mwt925" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_200-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-200" id="mwByc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwByg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByk">[</span>200<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByo">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBys">As of June 2025, Canberra's estimated population, including the whole of the ACT, was 484,630.<sup about="#mwt928" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABSGCCSA_8-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABSGCCSA"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABSGCCSA-8" id="mwByw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBy0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBy4">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBy8">]</span></span></a></sup> At the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Australian_census" title="2021 Australian census" about="#mwt926" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBzA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"CensusAU","href":"./Template:CensusAU"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2021"}},"i":0}}]}'>2021 census</a>, the population of the ACT was 453,558,<sup about="#mwt931" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_200-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:6-200"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-200" id="mwBzE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzM">[</span>200<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzQ">]</span></span></a></sup> while the population of the Canberra built-up area was 452,670, so 888 were located in the rural part of the ACT.<sup about="#mwt934" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2021_201-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Census2021-201"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2021-201" id="mwBzU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzc">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzg">]</span></span></a></sup> This was up from 395,790 at the 2016 census,<sup about="#mwt937" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2016_245-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2016"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Census2016-245"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2016-245" id="mwBzk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzs">[</span>245<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzw">]</span></span></a></sup> and 355,596 at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2011_Australian_census" title="2011 Australian census" about="#mwt927" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBz0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"CensusAU","href":"./Template:CensusAU"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2011"}},"i":0}}]}'>2011 census</a>.<sup about="#mwt940" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2011_246-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Census2011-246"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2011-246" id="mwBz4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBz8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0A">[</span>246<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0E">]</span></span></a></sup> Canberra has been the fastest-growing city in Australia in recent years, having grown 23.3% from 2011 to 2021.<sup about="#mwt941" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_200-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-200" id="mwB0I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0Q">[</span>200<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0U">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB0Y">Canberrans are relatively young, highly <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Population_mobility" title="Population mobility" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB0c">mobile</a> and well educated. In 2021, the median age was 35 years and only 13.8% of the population was aged over 65 years.<sup about="#mwt942" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2021_201-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2021-201" id="mwB0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0o">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0s">]</span></span></a></sup> Between 1996 and 2001, 61.9% of the population either moved to or from Canberra, which was the second highest mobility rate of any Australian capital city.<sup about="#mwt945" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-247" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-247"}}'><a href="#cite_note-247" id="mwB0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB00"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB04">[</span>247<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB08">]</span></span></a></sup> A 2024 report from the Australian Bureau of Statistics indicates that 49% of ACT residents aged 15–74 held a bachelor's degree or higher, the highest proportion among all Australian states and territories.<sup about="#mwt948" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-248" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248"}}'><a href="#cite_note-248" id="mwB1A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1I">[</span>248<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1M">]</span></span></a></sup> According to statistics collected by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Australia_Bank" title="National Australia Bank" id="mwB1Q">National Australia Bank</a>, Canberrans on average gave significantly more money to charity in 2014 than Australians in other states and territories, for both dollar giving and as a proportion of income.<sup about="#mwt951" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-249" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-249"}}'><a href="#cite_note-249" id="mwB1U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1c">[</span>249<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<table class="wikitable" style="float:right;" id="mwB1k">
<caption id="mwB1o">Country of birth (2021)<sup about="#mwt954" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au_250-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au-250"}}'><a href="#cite_note-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au-250" id="mwB1s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB10">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB14">]</span></span></a></sup></caption>
<tbody id="mwB18"><tr id="mwB2A"><th id="mwB2E">Birthplace<sup about="#mwt955" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-251" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"N"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-251"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"refn","href":"./Template:Refn"},"params":{"group":{"wt":"\"N\""},"1":{"wt":"In accordance with the Australian Bureau of Statistics source, [[England]], [[Scotland]], [[Mainland China]] and the Special Administrative Regions of [[Hong Kong]] and [[Macau]] are listed separately"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-251" data-mw-group="N" id="mwB2I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2Q">[</span>N 1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2U">]</span></span></a></sup></th><th id="mwB2Y">Population</th></tr>
<tr id="mwB2c">
<td id="mwB2g"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia" title="Australia" id="mwB2k">Australia</a></td><td id="mwB2o">306,896</td></tr>
<tr id="mwB2s">
<td id="mwB2w"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwB20">India</a></td><td id="mwB24">17,203<!-- England and Scotland are listed separately as per the source. Do not combine --></td></tr>
<tr id="mwB28">
<td id="mwB3A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/England" title="England" id="mwB3E">England</a></td>
<td id="mwB3I">13,245</td></tr>
<tr id="mwB3M">
<td id="mwB3Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwB3U">China</a> (including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_administrative_regions_of_China" title="Special administrative regions of China" id="mwB3Y">SARs</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan" title="Taiwan" id="mwB3c">Taiwan</a>)</td><td id="mwB3g">12,149<!-- Mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong and Macau SARs are listed separately as per the source. Do not combine --></td></tr>
<tr id="mwB3k">
<td id="mwB3o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepal" title="Nepal" id="mwB3s">Nepal</a></td><td id="mwB3w">5,689</td></tr>
<tr id="mwB30">
<td id="mwB34"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Zealand" title="New Zealand" id="mwB38">New Zealand</a></td><td id="mwB4A">5,122</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<p id="mwB4E">At the 2021 census, the most commonly nominated ancestries were:<sup about="#mwt958" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-252" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"N"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-252"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"refn","href":"./Template:Refn"},"params":{"group":{"wt":"\"N\""},"1":{"wt":"As a percentage of 373,561 persons who nominated their ancestry at the 2016 census."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-252" data-mw-group="N" id="mwB4I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4Q">[</span>N 2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4U">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt961" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au_250-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au"}}'><a href="#cite_note-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au-250" id="mwB4Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4g">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4k">]</span></span></a></sup> </p><!-- Only ancestries with &#x3E;1% are listed. Do not use the QuickStats data from ABS for ancestries. Use the full ancestry data series (eg from ABS Community Profiles series) as the QuickStats data shows each ancestry as a percentage of all ancestry responses (where each person can list up to two, thus a far greater number than the total population) while the full data series in the ABS Community Profiles show the percentage of people nominating a given ancestry as a percentage of the population who nominated an ancestry -->
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt962" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB4o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"columns-list","href":"./Template:Columns-list"},"params":{"colwidth":{"wt":"13em"},"1":{"wt":"\n*[[English Australians|English]] (32.0%)\n*[[Australians|Australian]] (31.5%){{refn|group=\"N\"|The Australian Bureau of Statistics has stated that most who nominate \"Australian\" as their ancestry are part of the [[Anglo-Celtic Australian|Anglo-Celtic]] group.&lt;ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.abs.gov.au/Ausstats/abs@.nsf/94713ad445ff1425ca25682000192af2/49f609c83cf34d69ca2569de0025c182!OpenDocument |title=Feature Article - Ethnic and Cultural Diversity in Australia |first=James |last=Jupp |website=www.abs.gov.au |date=January 1995 |access-date=16 June 2019 |archive-date=20 April 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160420205113/http://www.abs.gov.au/Ausstats/abs%40.nsf/94713ad445ff1425ca25682000192af2/49f609c83cf34d69ca2569de0025c182%21OpenDocument |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>}}\n*[[Irish Australians|Irish]] (11.6%)\n*[[Scottish Australians|Scottish]] (10.0%)\n*[[Chinese Australians|Chinese]] (5.7%)\n*[[Indigenous Australians|Indigenous]] (2.0%){{refn|group=\"N\"|name=ancestry|Of any ancestry. Includes those identifying as [[Aboriginal Australians]] or [[Torres Strait Islanders]]. Indigenous identification is separate to the ancestry question on the Australian Census and persons identifying as Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander may identify any ancestry.}}\n"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1184024115" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt963" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Div col/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .div-col{margin-top:0.3em;column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .div-col-small{font-size:90%}.mw-parser-output .div-col-rules{column-rule:1px solid #aaa}.mw-parser-output .div-col dl,.mw-parser-output .div-col ol,.mw-parser-output .div-col ul{margin-top:0}.mw-parser-output .div-col li,.mw-parser-output .div-col dd{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid-column}</style></span><div class="div-col   " style="column-width: 13em;" about="#mwt962" id="mwB4s">
<ul><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Australians" title="English Australians">English</a> (32.0%)</li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australians" title="Australians">Australian</a> (31.5%)<sup about="#mwt969" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-254" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"N"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-254"}}'><a href="#cite_note-254" data-mw-group="N" id="mwB4w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB40"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB44">[</span>N 3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB48">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irish_Australians" title="Irish Australians">Irish</a> (11.6%)</li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scottish_Australians" title="Scottish Australians">Scottish</a> (10.0%)</li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Australians" title="Chinese Australians">Chinese</a> (5.7%)</li>
<li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_Australians" title="Indigenous Australians">Indigenous</a> (2.0%)<sup about="#mwt973" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ancestry_255-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ancestry","group":"N"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ancestry-255"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ancestry-255" data-mw-group="N" id="mwB5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5I">[</span>N 4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5M">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></div>

<p id="mwB5Q">The 2021 census showed that 28.7% of Canberra's inhabitants were <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immigration_to_Australia" title="Immigration to Australia" id="mwB5U">born overseas</a>.<sup about="#mwt978" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au_250-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au"}}'><a href="#cite_note-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au-250" id="mwB5Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5g">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5k">]</span></span></a></sup> Of inhabitants born outside Australia, the most prevalent countries of birth were India, England, China and Nepal.<sup about="#mwt981" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-256" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-256"}}'><a href="#cite_note-256" id="mwB5o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5w">[</span>252<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB50">]</span></span></a></sup> 2.0% of the population, or 8,949 people, identified as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_Australians" title="Indigenous Australians" id="mwB54">Indigenous Australians</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aboriginal_Australians" title="Aboriginal Australians" id="mwB58">Aboriginal Australians</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torres_Strait_Islanders" title="Torres Strait Islanders" id="mwB6A">Torres Strait Islanders</a>) in 2021. This was an increase from 6,508 counted in 2016, and lower than the Australian percentage of 3.2% in 2021.<sup about="#mwt975" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ancestry_255-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ancestry","group":"N"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"refn","href":"./Template:Refn"},"params":{"group":{"wt":"\"N\""},"name":{"wt":"ancestry"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-ancestry-255" data-mw-group="N" id="mwB6E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6M">[</span>N 4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt982" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au_250-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au"}}'><a href="#cite_note-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au-250" id="mwB6U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6c">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB6k">At the 2021 census, 71.3% of people spoke only English at home, down from 72.7% in 2016. The other languages most commonly spoken at home were <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Mandarin" title="Standard Mandarin" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB6o">Mandarin</a> (3.2%), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepali_language" title="Nepali language" id="mwB6s">Nepali</a> (1.3%), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnamese_language" title="Vietnamese language" id="mwB6w">Vietnamese</a> (1.1%), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punjabi_language" title="Punjabi language" id="mwB60">Punjabi</a> (1.1%) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindi" title="Hindi" id="mwB64">Hindi</a> (1.0%).<sup about="#mwt983" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au_250-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au"}}'><a href="#cite_note-quickstats.censusdata.abs.gov.au-250" id="mwB68"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7E">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7I">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB7M">In 2021, the main religious affiliation in the ACT was Catholicism (19.3%), Anglicanism (8.2%) and Hinduism (4.5%). 43.5% described themselves as having no religion and 5.2 did not state a religion.<sup about="#mwt984" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2021_201-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2021-201" id="mwB7Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7Y">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7c">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwB7g" aria-labelledby="Culture"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Culture">Culture</h2></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwB7k" aria-labelledby="Education"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Education">Education</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt985" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB7o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Education in the Australian Capital Territory"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt986" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt985" id="mwB7s">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Education_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Education in the Australian Capital Territory">Education in the Australian Capital Territory</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB7w"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ANU_School_of_Art,_Canberra.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB70"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ANU_School_of_Art,_Canberra.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/ANU_School_of_Art%2C_Canberra.jpg/250px-ANU_School_of_Art%2C_Canberra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/ANU_School_of_Art%2C_Canberra.jpg/500px-ANU_School_of_Art%2C_Canberra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1000" data-file-height="742" data-file-type="bitmap" height="186" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB74"/></a><figcaption id="mwB78"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_National_University" title="Australian National University" id="mwB8A">ANU</a> School of Art (formerly the Canberra High School)</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwB8E">The two main tertiary institutions are the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_National_University" title="Australian National University" id="mwB8I">Australian National University</a> (ANU) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acton,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Acton, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB8M">Acton</a>, with over 10,200 undergraduate and over 7,100 postgraduate students,<sup about="#mwt992" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-anu_257-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"anu"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-anu-257"}}'><a href="#cite_note-anu-257" id="mwB8Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8Y">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8c">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Canberra" title="University of Canberra" id="mwB8g">University of Canberra</a> (UC) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Bruce, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB8k">Bruce</a>, with over 11,800 undergraduate and 6,300 postgraduate students.<sup about="#mwt995" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-uc_258-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"uc"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-uc-258"}}'><a href="#cite_note-uc-258" id="mwB8o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8w">[</span>254<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB80">]</span></span></a></sup> Established in 1946,<sup about="#mwt987" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGibbney1988258–262_259-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGibbney1988258–262"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGibbney1988258–262-259"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Gibbney"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"pp":{"wt":"258-262"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGibbney1988258–262-259" id="mwB84"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB88"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9A">[</span>255<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9E">]</span></span></a></sup> the ANU has always had a strong research focus and is ranked among the leading universities in the world and one of the best in Australia by the <i id="mwB9I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Times_Higher_Education_World_University_Rankings" title="Times Higher Education World University Rankings" id="mwB9M">Times Higher Education World University Rankings</a></i> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QS_World_University_Rankings" title="QS World University Rankings" id="mwB9Q">QS World University Rankings</a>.<sup about="#mwt996" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-anu_257-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"anu"}}'><a href="#cite_note-anu-257" id="mwB9U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9c">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9g">]</span></span></a></sup> There are two religious university campuses in Canberra: Signadou in the northern suburb of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watson,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Watson, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB9k">Watson</a> is a campus of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Catholic_University" title="Australian Catholic University" id="mwB9o">Australian Catholic University</a>;<sup about="#mwt999" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-260" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-260"}}'><a href="#cite_note-260" id="mwB9s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB90">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB94">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Mark's_National_Theological_Centre" title="St Mark's National Theological Centre" id="mwB98">St Mark's National Theological Centre</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barton,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Barton, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB-A">Barton</a> is part of the secular <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Sturt_University" title="Charles Sturt University" id="mwB-E">Charles Sturt University</a>.<sup about="#mwt1002" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-261" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-261"}}'><a href="#cite_note-261" id="mwB-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-Q">[</span>257<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-U">]</span></span></a></sup> The ACT Government announced on 5 March 2020 that the CIT campus and an adjoining carpark in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reid,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Reid, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB-Y">Reid</a> would be leased to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_New_South_Wales" title="University of New South Wales" id="mwB-c">University of New South Wales</a> (UNSW) for a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppercorn_lease" title="Peppercorn lease" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-g">peppercorn lease</a>, for it to develop as a campus for a new UNSW Canberra.<sup about="#mwt1005" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2020-03-05_ABC_262-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"2020-03-05_ABC"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2020-03-05_ABC-262"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2020-03-05_ABC-262" id="mwB-k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-s">[</span>258<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-w">]</span></span></a></sup> UNSW released a master plan in 2021 for a 6,000 student campus to be realised over 15 years at a cost of $1 billion.<sup about="#mwt1008" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-263" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-263"}}'><a href="#cite_note-263" id="mwB-0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-8">[</span>259<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB_E">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Defence_College" title="Australian Defence College" id="mwB_I">Australian Defence College</a> has two campuses: the Australian Command and Staff College (ACSC) plus the Centre for Defence and Strategic Studies (CDSS) at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weston,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Weston, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB_M">Weston</a>, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Defence_Force_Academy" title="Australian Defence Force Academy" id="mwB_Q">Australian Defence Force Academy</a> (ADFA) beside the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Military_College,_Duntroon" title="Royal Military College, Duntroon" id="mwB_U">Royal Military College, Duntroon</a> located in the inner-northern suburb of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campbell,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Campbell, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwB_Y">Campbell</a>.<sup about="#mwt1011" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-264" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-264"}}'><a href="#cite_note-264" id="mwB_c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_k">[</span>260<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1014" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-265" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-265"}}'><a href="#cite_note-265" id="mwB_s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_0">[</span>261<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_4">]</span></span></a></sup> ADFA teaches military undergraduates and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quaternary_education" title="Quaternary education" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB_8">postgraduates</a> and includes UNSW Canberra at ADFA, a campus of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_New_South_Wales" title="University of New South Wales" id="mwCAA">University of New South Wales</a>.<sup about="#mwt1017" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-266" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-266"}}'><a href="#cite_note-266" id="mwCAE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAM">[</span>262<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Duntroon provides <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Army" title="Australian Army" id="mwCAU">Australian Army</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Officer_(armed_forces)" title="Officer (armed forces)" id="mwCAY">officer</a> training.<sup about="#mwt1020" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-267" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-267"}}'><a href="#cite_note-267" id="mwCAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAk">[</span>263<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCAs">Tertiary level vocational education is also available through the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Institute_of_Technology" title="Canberra Institute of Technology" id="mwCAw">Canberra Institute of Technology</a> (CIT), with campuses in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Bruce, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCA0">Bruce</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woden_Valley" title="Woden Valley" id="mwCA4">Woden</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gungahlin" title="Gungahlin" id="mwCA8">Gungahlin</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuggeranong" title="Tuggeranong" id="mwCBA">Tuggeranong</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyshwick" title="Fyshwick" id="mwCBE">Fyshwick</a>.<sup about="#mwt1023" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-268" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-268"}}'><a href="#cite_note-268" id="mwCBI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBQ">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBU">]</span></span></a></sup> The combined enrolment of the CIT campuses was about 20,000 students students in 2023.<sup about="#mwt1026" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-269" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-269"}}'><a href="#cite_note-269" id="mwCBY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBg">[</span>265<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBk">]</span></span></a></sup> Following the transfer of land in Reid for the new UNSW Canberra, a new CIT campus in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woden_Valley" title="Woden Valley" id="mwCBo">Woden</a> was completed in July 2025.<sup about="#mwt1029" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-270" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-270"}}'><a href="#cite_note-270" id="mwCBs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCB0">[</span>266<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCB4">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2016 there were 140 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_schools_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="List of schools in the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCB8">schools</a> in Canberra; 93 were operated by the government and 47 were private.<sup about="#mwt1032" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-271" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-271"}}'><a href="#cite_note-271" id="mwCCA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCI">[</span>267<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1035" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-272" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-272"}}'><a href="#cite_note-272" id="mwCCQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCY">[</span>268<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCc">]</span></span></a></sup> Canberra also has the highest percentage of non-government (private) school students in Australia, accounting for 40.6<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCCg"> </span>per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCCk"> </span>cent of ACT enrolments.<sup about="#mwt1038" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-273" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-273"}}'><a href="#cite_note-273" id="mwCCo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCw">[</span>269<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCC0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="20" id="mwCC4" aria-labelledby="Arts,_entertainment_and_events"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Arts,_entertainment_and_events"><span id="Arts.2C_entertainment_and_events" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Arts, entertainment and events</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1039" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCC8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Music of Canberra"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1040" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1039" id="mwCDA">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Canberra" title="Music of Canberra">Music of Canberra</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCDE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:National_Film_and_Sound_Archive,_Canberra,_2022,_03_(2).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCDI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:National_Film_and_Sound_Archive,_Canberra,_2022,_03_(2).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/National_Film_and_Sound_Archive%2C_Canberra%2C_2022%2C_03_%282%29.jpg/250px-National_Film_and_Sound_Archive%2C_Canberra%2C_2022%2C_03_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/National_Film_and_Sound_Archive%2C_Canberra%2C_2022%2C_03_%282%29.jpg/500px-National_Film_and_Sound_Archive%2C_Canberra%2C_2022%2C_03_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2763" data-file-height="1841" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCDM"/></a><figcaption id="mwCDQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Film_and_Sound_Archive" title="National Film and Sound Archive" id="mwCDU">National Film and Sound Archive</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCDY">Canberra is home to many national monuments and institutions such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliament_House,_Canberra" title="Parliament House, Canberra" id="mwCDc">Parliament House</a>,<sup about="#mwt1049" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-274" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-274"}}'><a href="#cite_note-274" id="mwCDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDo">[</span>270<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDs">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Court_of_Australia" title="High Court of Australia" id="mwCDw">High Court</a><sup about="#mwt1052" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-275" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-275"}}'><a href="#cite_note-275" id="mwCD0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCD4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCD8">[</span>271<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEA">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Gallery_of_Australia" title="National Gallery of Australia" id="mwCEE">National Gallery of Australia</a>,<sup about="#mwt1055" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-276" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-276"}}'><a href="#cite_note-276" id="mwCEI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEQ">[</span>272<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEU">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Portrait_Gallery_(Australia)" title="National Portrait Gallery (Australia)" id="mwCEY">National Portrait Gallery</a>,<sup about="#mwt1058" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-277" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-277"}}'><a href="#cite_note-277" id="mwCEc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEk">[</span>273<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEo">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Library_of_Australia" title="National Library of Australia" id="mwCEs">National Library</a>,<sup about="#mwt1061" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-278" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-278"}}'><a href="#cite_note-278" id="mwCEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCE0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCE4">[</span>274<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCE8">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Archives_of_Australia" title="National Archives of Australia" id="mwCFA">National Archives</a>,<sup about="#mwt1064" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-279" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-279"}}'><a href="#cite_note-279" id="mwCFE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFM">[</span>275<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Questacon" title="Questacon" id="mwCFU">Questacon</a><sup about="#mwt1067" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-280" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-280"}}'><a href="#cite_note-280" id="mwCFY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFg">[</span>276<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFk">]</span></span></a></sup> and the Museum of Australian Democracy at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Parliament_House,_Canberra" title="Old Parliament House, Canberra" id="mwCFo">Old Parliament House</a>,<sup about="#mwt1070" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-281" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-281"}}'><a href="#cite_note-281" id="mwCFs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF0">[</span>277<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF4">]</span></span></a></sup> all lying in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliamentary_Triangle,_Canberra" title="Parliamentary Triangle, Canberra" id="mwCF8">Parliamentary Triangle</a>.<sup about="#mwt1041" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215_282-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"pp":{"wt":"214-215"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282" id="mwCGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGI">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1071" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-map_176-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"map"}}'><a href="#cite_note-map-176" id="mwCGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGY">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGc">]</span></span></a></sup> Many Commonwealth government buildings in Canberra are open to the public, including Parliament House, the High Court and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Australian_Mint" title="Royal Australian Mint" id="mwCGg">Royal Australian Mint</a>.<sup about="#mwt1074" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-283" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-283"}}'><a href="#cite_note-283" id="mwCGk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGs">[</span>279<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGw">]</span></span></a></sup> Nearby, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campbell,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Campbell, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCG0">Campbell</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acton,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Acton, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCG4">Acton</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Civic, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCG8">Civic</a> are the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_War_Memorial" title="Australian War Memorial" id="mwCHA">Australian War Memorial</a>,<sup about="#mwt1077" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-284" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-284"}}'><a href="#cite_note-284" id="mwCHE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHM">[</span>280<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHQ">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Academy_of_Science" title="Australian Academy of Science" id="mwCHU">Australian Academy of Science</a>,<sup about="#mwt1080" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-285" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-285"}}'><a href="#cite_note-285" id="mwCHY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHg">[</span>281<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHk">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Film_and_Sound_Archive" title="National Film and Sound Archive" id="mwCHo">National Film and Sound Archive</a>,<sup about="#mwt1083" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-286" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-286"}}'><a href="#cite_note-286" id="mwCHs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCH0">[</span>282<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCH4">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Museum_of_Australia" title="National Museum of Australia" id="mwCH8">National Museum</a><sup about="#mwt1086" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-287" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-287"}}'><a href="#cite_note-287" id="mwCIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCII">[</span>283<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIM">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Institute_of_Aboriginal_and_Torres_Strait_Islander_Studies" title="Australian Institute of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Studies" id="mwCIQ">Australian Institute of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Studies</a>.<sup about="#mwt1089" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-288" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-288"}}'><a href="#cite_note-288" id="mwCIU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIc">[</span>284<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1044" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215_282-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"pp":{"wt":"214-215"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282" id="mwCIk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIs">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1090" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-map_176-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"map"}}'><a href="#cite_note-map-176" id="mwCI0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCI4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI8">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCJE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NatMusAus_Main_Entrance_Strip.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCJI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NatMusAus_Main_Entrance_Strip.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/NatMusAus_Main_Entrance_Strip.jpg/250px-NatMusAus_Main_Entrance_Strip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/NatMusAus_Main_Entrance_Strip.jpg/500px-NatMusAus_Main_Entrance_Strip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1500" data-file-height="1125" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCJM"/></a><figcaption id="mwCJQ">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Museum_of_Australia" title="National Museum of Australia" id="mwCJU">National Museum of Australia</a> established in 2001 records Australia's social history and is one of Canberra's more architecturally daring buildings.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCJY">Lake Burley Griffin is the site of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_James_Cook_Memorial" title="Captain James Cook Memorial" id="mwCJc">Captain James Cook Memorial</a><sup about="#mwt1108" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-289" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-289"}}'><a href="#cite_note-289" id="mwCJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJo">[</span>285<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJs">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Carillon" title="National Carillon" id="mwCJw">National Carillon</a>.<sup about="#mwt1111" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-290" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-290"}}'><a href="#cite_note-290" id="mwCJ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJ8">[</span>286<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKA">]</span></span></a></sup> Other sites in the Parliamentary Triangle are<sup about="#mwt1091" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215_282-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"pp":{"wt":"214-215"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282" id="mwCKE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKM">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1114" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-map_176-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"map"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-map-176"}}'><a href="#cite_note-map-176" id="mwCKU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKc">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Place,_Canberra" title="Commonwealth Place, Canberra" id="mwCKk">Commonwealth Place</a>,<sup about="#mwt1117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-291" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-291"}}'><a href="#cite_note-291" id="mwCKo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKw">[</span>287<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCK0">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reconciliation_Place" title="Reconciliation Place" id="mwCK4">Reconciliation Place</a><sup about="#mwt1120" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-292" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-292"}}'><a href="#cite_note-292" id="mwCK8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLE">[</span>288<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLI">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Park" title="Commonwealth Park" id="mwCLM">Commonwealth Park</a>,<sup about="#mwt1123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-293" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-293"}}'><a href="#cite_note-293" id="mwCLQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLY">[</span>289<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLc">]</span></span></a></sup> which is the site of Canberra's annual <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floriade_(Canberra)" title="Floriade (Canberra)" id="mwCLg">Floriade</a>. This is the largest flower festival in the Southern Hemisphere and features a large display of flowers every Spring.<sup about="#mwt1126" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-294" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-294"}}'><a href="#cite_note-294" id="mwCLk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLs">[</span>290<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1129" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-295" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-295"}}'><a href="#cite_note-295" id="mwCL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCL8">[</span>291<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1094" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024220_296-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024220"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024220-296"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"p":{"wt":"220"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024220-296" id="mwCME"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCMI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMM">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Balloon_Spectacular" title="Canberra Balloon Spectacular" id="mwCMU">Canberra Balloon Spectacular</a> is held in March on the Patrick White Lawns, next to the National Library.<sup about="#mwt1132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-297" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-297"}}'><a href="#cite_note-297" id="mwCMY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCMc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMg">[</span>293<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1097" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024220_296-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024220"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024220-296"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"p":{"wt":"220"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024220-296" id="mwCMo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCMs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMw">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCM0">]</span></span></a></sup> Located to the north of the lake are the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_National_Botanic_Gardens" title="Australian National Botanic Gardens" id="mwCM4">Australian National Botanic Gardens</a>,<sup about="#mwt1135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-298" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-298"}}'><a href="#cite_note-298" id="mwCM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNE">[</span>294<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNI">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian–American_Memorial" title="Australian–American Memorial" id="mwCNM">Australian–American Memorial</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anzac_Parade,_Canberra" title="Anzac Parade, Canberra" id="mwCNQ">Anzac Parade</a>, which is lined by several memorials,<sup about="#mwt1138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-299" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-299"}}'><a href="#cite_note-299" id="mwCNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNc">[</span>295<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-map_176-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"map"}}'><a href="#cite_note-map-176" id="mwCNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNs">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215_282-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"pp":{"wt":"214-215"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024214–215-282" id="mwCN0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCN4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCN8">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOA">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Arboretum_Canberra" title="National Arboretum Canberra" id="mwCOE">National Arboretum</a><sup about="#mwt1142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-300" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-300"}}'><a href="#cite_note-300" id="mwCOI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOQ">[</span>296<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024220_296-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024220"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024220-296"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"p":{"wt":"220"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024220-296" id="mwCOY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOg">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOk">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Zoo_and_Aquarium" title="National Zoo and Aquarium" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCOo">National Zoo and Aquarium</a>.<sup about="#mwt1145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-301" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-301"}}'><a href="#cite_note-301" id="mwCOs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCO0">[</span>297<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCO4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCO8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2015-09-18_Floriade_Canberra_2015_-_2.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCPA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2015-09-18_Floriade_Canberra_2015_-_2.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/2015-09-18_Floriade_Canberra_2015_-_2.jpg/250px-2015-09-18_Floriade_Canberra_2015_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/2015-09-18_Floriade_Canberra_2015_-_2.jpg/500px-2015-09-18_Floriade_Canberra_2015_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5184" data-file-height="3287" data-file-type="bitmap" height="159" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCPE"/></a><figcaption id="mwCPI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floriade_(Canberra)" title="Floriade (Canberra)" id="mwCPM">Floriade</a> is held in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Park" title="Commonwealth Park" id="mwCPQ">Commonwealth Park</a> every spring. It is the largest flower festival in the Southern Hemisphere.<sup about="#mwt1148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-floriadeaustralia_302-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"floriadeaustralia"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-floriadeaustralia-302"}}'><a href="#cite_note-floriadeaustralia-302" id="mwCPU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPc">[</span>298<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPg">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwCPk">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Museum_and_Gallery" title="Canberra Museum and Gallery" id="mwCPo">Canberra Museum and Gallery</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civic,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Civic, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCPs">the city</a> is a repository of local history and art, housing a permanent collection and visiting exhibitions.<sup about="#mwt1151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-303" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-303"}}'><a href="#cite_note-303" id="mwCPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCP4">[</span>299<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCP8">]</span></span></a></sup> Several historic homes are open to the public: Lanyon and Tuggeranong Homesteads in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuggeranong" title="Tuggeranong" id="mwCQA">Tuggeranong Valley</a>,<sup about="#mwt1154" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-304" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-304"}}'><a href="#cite_note-304" id="mwCQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQM">[</span>300<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-305" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-305"}}'><a href="#cite_note-305" id="mwCQU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQc">[</span>301<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQg">]</span></span></a></sup> Mugga-Mugga in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symonston,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Symonston, Australian Capital Territory" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCQk">Symonston</a>,<sup about="#mwt1160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-306" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-306"}}'><a href="#cite_note-306" id="mwCQo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQw">[</span>302<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQ0">]</span></span></a></sup> and Blundells' Cottage in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkes,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Parkes, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCQ4">Parkes</a> all display the lifestyle of the early European settlers.<sup about="#mwt1161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BLUNDELL_30-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BLUNDELL"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BLUNDELL-30" id="mwCQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRE">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRI">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calthorpes'_House" title="Calthorpes' House" id="mwCRM">Calthorpes' House</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Hill,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Red Hill, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCRQ">Red Hill</a> is a well-preserved example of a 1920s house from Canberra's very early days.<sup about="#mwt1164" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-307" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-307"}}'><a href="#cite_note-307" id="mwCRU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRc">[</span>303<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strathnairn_Homestead,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Strathnairn Homestead, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCRk">Strathnairn Homestead</a> is an historic building which also dates from the 1920s.<sup about="#mwt1167" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-308" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-308"}}'><a href="#cite_note-308" id="mwCRo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRw">[</span>304<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCR0">]</span></span></a></sup> The Schoolhouse Museum at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_John_the_Baptist_Church,_Reid" title="St John the Baptist Church, Reid" id="mwCR4">St John's Anglican Church</a> in Reid showcases school life in the 1840s.<sup about="#mwt1170" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-309" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-309"}}'><a href="#cite_note-309" id="mwCR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSE">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCSM"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra_at_Llewellyn_Hall_April_2022.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCSQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra_at_Llewellyn_Hall_April_2022.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra_at_Llewellyn_Hall_April_2022.jpg/250px-Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra_at_Llewellyn_Hall_April_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra_at_Llewellyn_Hall_April_2022.jpg/500px-Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra_at_Llewellyn_Hall_April_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3652" data-file-height="2283" data-file-type="bitmap" height="156" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCSU"/></a><figcaption id="mwCSY">Llewellyn Hall is home to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Symphony_Orchestra" title="Canberra Symphony Orchestra" id="mwCSc">Canberra Symphony Orchestra</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCSg">Canberra has many venues for live music and theatre: the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Theatre" title="Canberra Theatre" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCSk">Canberra Theatre and Playhouse</a> which hosts many major concerts and productions;<sup about="#mwt1173" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-310" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-310"}}'><a href="#cite_note-310" id="mwCSo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSw">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCS0">]</span></span></a></sup> and Llewellyn Hall (within the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ANU_School_of_Music" title="ANU School of Music" id="mwCS4">ANU School of Music</a>), a world-class concert hall are two of the most notable.<sup about="#mwt1176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rg_311-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rg"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-rg-311"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rg-311" id="mwCS8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTE">[</span>307<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTI">]</span></span></a></sup> The Street Theatre is a venue with less mainstream offerings.<sup about="#mwt1177" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rg_311-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rg"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rg-311" id="mwCTM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTU">[</span>307<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTY">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Hall,_Canberra" title="Albert Hall, Canberra" id="mwCTc">The Albert Hall</a> was the city's first performing arts venue, opened in 1928. It was the original performance venue for theatre groups such as the Canberra Repertory Society.<sup about="#mwt1180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-312" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-312"}}'><a href="#cite_note-312" id="mwCTg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTo">[</span>308<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCTw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Skyfire_2017_(203911129).jpeg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCT0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Skyfire_2017_(203911129).jpeg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Canberra_Skyfire_2017_%28203911129%29.jpeg/250px-Canberra_Skyfire_2017_%28203911129%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Canberra_Skyfire_2017_%28203911129%29.jpeg/500px-Canberra_Skyfire_2017_%28203911129%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1366" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCT4"/></a><figcaption id="mwCT8">The annual Skyfire fireworks display over Lake Burley Griffin, held during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enlighten_Canberra" title="Enlighten Canberra" id="mwCUA">Enlighten Festival</a></figcaption></figure><p id="mwCUE">

There are numerous bars and nightclubs which also offer live entertainment, particularly concentrated in the areas of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="City, Australian Capital Territory" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCUI">the city</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Braddon,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Braddon, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCUM">Braddon</a>.<sup about="#mwt1181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReid2024212–220_313-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEReid2024212–220"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024212–220-313"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Reid"},"2":{"wt":"2024"},"pp":{"wt":"212-220"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReid2024212–220-313" id="mwCUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCUU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUY">[</span>309<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUc">]</span></span></a></sup> All town centres have a library.<sup about="#mwt1186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-314" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-314"}}'><a href="#cite_note-314" id="mwCUg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCUk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUo">[</span>310<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUs">]</span></span></a></sup> Popular cultural events include the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Folk_Festival_(Australia)" title="National Folk Festival (Australia)" id="mwCUw">National Folk Festival</a>,<sup about="#mwt1189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-315" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-315"}}'><a href="#cite_note-315" id="mwCU0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCU4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCU8">[</span>311<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVA">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Canberra_Show" title="Royal Canberra Show" id="mwCVE">Royal Canberra Show</a>,<sup about="#mwt1192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-316" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-316"}}'><a href="#cite_note-316" id="mwCVI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVQ">[</span>312<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVU">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summernats" title="Summernats" id="mwCVY">Summernats</a> car festival,<sup about="#mwt1195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-317" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-317"}}'><a href="#cite_note-317" id="mwCVc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVk">[</span>313<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVo">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enlighten_Canberra" title="Enlighten Canberra" id="mwCVs">Enlighten</a> festival<sup about="#mwt1198" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-318" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-318"}}'><a href="#cite_note-318" id="mwCVw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCV0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCV4">[</span>314<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCV8">]</span></span></a></sup> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Multicultural_Festival" title="National Multicultural Festival" id="mwCWA">National Multicultural Festival</a> in February.<sup about="#mwt1201" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-319" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-319"}}'><a href="#cite_note-319" id="mwCWE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCWI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWM">[</span>315<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Dinosaur_Museum" title="National Dinosaur Museum" id="mwCWU">National Dinosaur Museum</a> is located on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barton_Highway" title="Barton Highway" id="mwCWY">Barton Highway</a> north of Canberra.<sup about="#mwt1204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-320" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-320"}}'><a href="#cite_note-320" id="mwCWc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCWg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWk">[</span>316<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWo">]</span></span></a></sup></p><figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCWs"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:War_memorial_01.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCWw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:War_memorial_01.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/War_memorial_01.jpg/250px-War_memorial_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/War_memorial_01.jpg/500px-War_memorial_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1178" data-file-height="941" data-file-type="bitmap" height="200" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCW0"/></a><figcaption id="mwCW4">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_War_Memorial" title="Australian War Memorial" id="mwCW8">Australian War Memorial</a></figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwCXA" aria-labelledby="Media"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Media">Media</h3></div>
<p id="mwCXE">As Australia's capital, Canberra is the most important centre for much of Australia's political reportage and thus all the major media, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Broadcasting_Corporation" title="Australian Broadcasting Corporation" id="mwCXI">Australian Broadcasting Corporation</a>, the commercial television networks, and the metropolitan newspapers maintain local bureaus. News organisations are represented in the <i id="mwCXM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Press_Gallery" title="Canberra Press Gallery" id="mwCXQ">press gallery</a></i>, a group of journalists who report on the national <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parliament_of_Australia" title="Parliament of Australia" id="mwCXU">parliament</a>.<sup about="#mwt1210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-321" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-321"}}'><a href="#cite_note-321" id="mwCXY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCXc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXg">[</span>317<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXk">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Press_Club_of_Australia" title="National Press Club of Australia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCXo">The National Press Club of Australia</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barton,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Barton, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCXs">Barton</a> has regular television broadcasts of its lunches at which a prominent guest, typically a politician or other public figure, delivers a speech followed by a question-and-answer session.<sup about="#mwt1213" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-322" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-322"}}'><a href="#cite_note-322" id="mwCXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCX0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCX4">[</span>318<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCX8">]</span></span></a></sup> Canberra has a daily newspaper, <i id="mwCYA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Canberra_Times" title="The Canberra Times" id="mwCYE">The Canberra Times</a></i>, which was established in 1926.<sup about="#mwt1205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWigmore197187_323-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEWigmore197187"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197187-323"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Wigmore"},"2":{"wt":"1971"},"p":{"wt":"87"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWigmore197187-323" id="mwCYI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYQ">[</span>319<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1216" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-324" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-324"}}'><a href="#cite_note-324" id="mwCYY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYg">[</span>320<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYk">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwCYo">There are a number of AM and FM stations broadcasting in Canberra (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_radio_station_callsigns_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="List of radio station callsigns in the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCYs">AM/FM Listing</a>). Commercial operators include the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_Radio_Network" title="Capital Radio Network" id="mwCYw">Capital Radio Network</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2CA" title="2CA" id="mwCY0">2CA</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2CC" title="2CC" id="mwCY4">2CC</a>), and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austereo" title="Austereo" id="mwCY8">Austereo</a>/<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Radio_Network" title="Australian Radio Network" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCZA">ARN</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/104.7_(Canberra)" title="104.7 (Canberra)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCZE">104.7</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mix_106.3" title="Mix 106.3" id="mwCZI">Mix 106.3</a>). There are also several community operated stations.<sup about="#mwt1219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-325" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-325"}}'><a href="#cite_note-325" id="mwCZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZU">[</span>321<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZY">]</span></span></a></sup> Each of Australia's three commercial television networks and two public broadcasters broadcast in Canberra, each over a primary channel and several <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_terrestrial_television_in_Australia#Additional_channels" title="Digital terrestrial television in Australia" id="mwCZc">multichannels</a>.<sup about="#mwt1222" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-326" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-326"}}'><a href="#cite_note-326" id="mwCZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZo">[</span>322<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<ul id="mwCZw"><li id="mwCZ0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ABC_Television_(Australian_TV_network)" title="ABC Television (Australian TV network)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCZ4">ABC</a> Canberra (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ABC_Canberra_(TV_station)" title="ABC Canberra (TV station)" id="mwCZ8">ABC</a>)</li>
<li id="mwCaA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_Broadcasting_Service" title="Special Broadcasting Service" id="mwCaE">SBS</a> New South Wales (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SBS_(Australian_TV_channel)" title="SBS (Australian TV channel)" id="mwCaI">SBS</a>)</li>
<li id="mwCaM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_10" title="Network 10" id="mwCaQ">Network 10</a> Southern NSW &amp; ACT (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CTC_(TV_station)" title="CTC (TV station)" id="mwCaU">CTC</a>) – <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_10" title="Network 10" id="mwCaY">Network 10</a> owned and operated station</li>
<li id="mwCac"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Network" title="Seven Network" id="mwCag">Seven Network</a> Southern NSW &amp; ACT (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CBN_(Australian_TV_station)" title="CBN (Australian TV station)" id="mwCak">CBN</a>) – <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Network" title="Seven Network" id="mwCao">Seven Network</a> owned and operated station</li>
<li id="mwCas"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WIN_Television" title="WIN Television" id="mwCaw">WIN Television</a> Southern NSW &amp; ACT (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WIN_(TV_station)" title="WIN (TV station)" id="mwCa0">WIN</a>) – <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nine_Network" title="Nine Network" id="mwCa4">Nine Network</a> affiliate</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwCa8" aria-labelledby="Sport"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Sport">Sport</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1223" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCbA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sport in the Australian Capital Territory"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1224" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1223" id="mwCbE">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sport_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Sport in the Australian Capital Territory">Sport in the Australian Capital Territory</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCbI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BruceStadium19032005.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCbM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BruceStadium19032005.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/BruceStadium19032005.JPG/250px-BruceStadium19032005.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/BruceStadium19032005.JPG/500px-BruceStadium19032005.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1280" data-file-height="960" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCbQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwCbU">A rugby league match at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Stadium" title="Canberra Stadium" id="mwCbY">Canberra Stadium</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwCbc">In addition to local sporting leagues, Canberra has a number of sporting teams that compete in national and international competitions. The best known teams are the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Raiders" title="Canberra Raiders" id="mwCbg">Canberra Raiders</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACT_Brumbies" title="ACT Brumbies" id="mwCbk">ACT Brumbies</a> who play <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugby_league" title="Rugby league" id="mwCbo">rugby league</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugby_union" title="Rugby union" id="mwCbs">rugby union</a> respectively; both have been champions of their leagues.<sup about="#mwt1227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-327" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-327"}}'><a href="#cite_note-327" id="mwCbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCb0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCb4">[</span>323<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCb8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-328" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-328"}}'><a href="#cite_note-328" id="mwCcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCcE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcI">[</span>324<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcM">]</span></span></a></sup> Both teams play their home games at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Stadium" title="Canberra Stadium" id="mwCcQ">Canberra Stadium</a>,<sup about="#mwt1233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-329" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-329"}}'><a href="#cite_note-329" id="mwCcU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCcY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcc">[</span>325<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcg">]</span></span></a></sup> which was used to hold group matches in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_football" title="Association football" id="mwCck">football</a> for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_Summer_Olympics" title="2000 Summer Olympics" id="mwCco">2000 Summer Olympics</a><sup about="#mwt1236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-330" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-330"}}'><a href="#cite_note-330" id="mwCcs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCcw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCc0">[</span>326<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCc4">]</span></span></a></sup> and in rugby union for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2003_Rugby_World_Cup" title="2003 Rugby World Cup" id="mwCc8">2003 Rugby World Cup</a>.<sup about="#mwt1239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-331" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-331"}}'><a href="#cite_note-331" id="mwCdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdI">[</span>327<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdM">]</span></span></a></sup> 
<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_United_FC" title="Canberra United FC" id="mwCdQ">Canberra United</a> represents the city in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A-League_Women" title="A-League Women" id="mwCdU">A-League Women</a> (formerly the W-League), the national <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women's_association_football" title="Women's association football" id="mwCdY">women's soccer</a> league and were champions in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_W-League_(Australia)" title="2014 W-League (Australia)" id="mwCdc">2014</a>.<sup about="#mwt1245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-332" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-332"}}'><a href="#cite_note-332" id="mwCdg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdo">[</span>328<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCds">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_rules_football_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Australian rules football in the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCdw">ACT division</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Football_League" title="Australian Football League" id="mwCd0">Australian Football League</a> bid for a club for the national competition in 1981.<sup about="#mwt1248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-333" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-333"}}'><a href="#cite_note-333" id="mwCd4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCd8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeA">[</span>329<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeE">]</span></span></a></sup> The league has rejected numerous such proposals over the years and, since 2013, it has designated Canberra as being represented by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Western_Sydney_Giants" title="Greater Western Sydney Giants" id="mwCeI">Greater Western Sydney Giants</a>,<sup about="#mwt1251" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-334" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-334"}}'><a href="#cite_note-334" id="mwCeM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCeQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeU">[</span>330<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeY">]</span></span></a></sup> which has played three home games at Manuka Oval each season since 2013<sup about="#mwt1254" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GIANTS_add_gold_for_Canberra_335-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GIANTS add gold for Canberra"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-GIANTS_add_gold_for_Canberra-335"}}'><a href="#cite_note-GIANTS_add_gold_for_Canberra-335" id="mwCec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCek">[</span>331<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeo">]</span></span></a></sup> with support from the ACT Government.<sup about="#mwt1257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-336" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-336"}}'><a href="#cite_note-336" id="mwCes"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCe0">[</span>332<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCe4">]</span></span></a></sup> The city also has a successful basketball team, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Capitals" title="Canberra Capitals" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCe8">Canberra Capitals</a>, which has won nine <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women's_National_Basketball_League" title="Women's National Basketball League" id="mwCfA">national women's basketball</a> titles, most recently in 2019–20.<sup about="#mwt1260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-337" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-337"}}'><a href="#cite_note-337" id="mwCfE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfM">[</span>333<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The historic <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister's_XI" title="Prime Minister's XI" id="mwCfU">Prime Minister's XI</a> cricket match is played at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuka_Oval" title="Manuka Oval" id="mwCfY">Manuka Oval</a> annually.<sup about="#mwt1240" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGrowden2008200–210_338-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGrowden2008200–210"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGrowden2008200–210-338"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Growden"},"2":{"wt":"2008"},"pp":{"wt":"200-210"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGrowden2008200–210-338" id="mwCfc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfk">[</span>334<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfo">]</span></span></a></sup> Other significant annual sporting events include the annual <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Marathon" title="Canberra Marathon" id="mwCfs">Canberra Marathon</a>, established in 1976,<sup about="#mwt1263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Canberra_Marathon_339-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Canberra Marathon"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Canberra_Marathon-339"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Canberra_Marathon-339" id="mwCfw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCf0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCf4">[</span>335<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCf8">]</span></span></a></sup> and the Challenge Canberra middle distance triathlon race was established in 2023.<sup about="#mwt1266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-340" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-340"}}'><a href="#cite_note-340" id="mwCgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgI">[</span>336<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgM">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Tennis_International" title="Canberra Tennis International" id="mwCgQ">Canberra Tennis International</a> has been held at the Canberra Tennis Centre, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyneham,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Lyneham, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCgU">Lyneham</a> since 2015,<sup about="#mwt1269" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-341" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-341"}}'><a href="#cite_note-341" id="mwCgY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgg">[</span>337<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgk">]</span></span></a></sup> usually annually.<sup about="#mwt1272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-342" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-342"}}'><a href="#cite_note-342" id="mwCgo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgw">[</span>338<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCg0">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCg4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:PM's_11_Cricket_at_Manuka_Oval.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCg8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:PM's_11_Cricket_at_Manuka_Oval.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/PM%27s_11_Cricket_at_Manuka_Oval.jpg/250px-PM%27s_11_Cricket_at_Manuka_Oval.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/PM%27s_11_Cricket_at_Manuka_Oval.jpg/500px-PM%27s_11_Cricket_at_Manuka_Oval.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="2138" data-file-type="bitmap" height="133" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwChA"/></a><figcaption id="mwChE">The annual Prime Minister's XI cricket match at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuka_Oval" title="Manuka Oval" id="mwChI">Manuka Oval</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwChM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Institute_of_Sport" title="Australian Institute of Sport" id="mwChQ">Australian Institute of Sport</a> (AIS) is located in the Canberra suburb of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Bruce, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwChU">Bruce</a>.<sup about="#mwt1273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988304_343-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988304"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988304-343"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"304"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988304-343" id="mwChY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwChc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChg">[</span>339<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChk">]</span></span></a></sup> The AIS is a specialised educational and training institution providing coaching for elite junior and senior athletes in a number of sports. The AIS has been operating since 1981 and has achieved significant success in producing elite athletes, both local and international.<sup about="#mwt1276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESparke1988304_343-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESparke1988304"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988304-343"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sparke"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"304"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESparke1988304-343" id="mwCho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwChs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChw">[</span>339<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCh0">]</span></span></a></sup> The majority of Australia's team members and medallists at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_Summer_Olympics" title="2000 Summer Olympics" id="mwCh4">2000 Summer Olympics</a> in Sydney were AIS graduates.<sup about="#mwt1281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-344" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-344"}}'><a href="#cite_note-344" id="mwCh8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCiA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiE">[</span>340<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiI">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwCiM">A Canberra-wide series of bicycle paths are available to cyclists for recreational and sporting purposes.<sup about="#mwt1284" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-345" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-345"}}'><a href="#cite_note-345" id="mwCiQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCiU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiY">[</span>341<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCic">]</span></span></a></sup> Canberra Nature Parks have a large range of walking paths, horse and mountain bike trails.<sup about="#mwt1287" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-346" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-346"}}'><a href="#cite_note-346" id="mwCig"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCik"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCio">[</span>342<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCis">]</span></span></a></sup> Water sports like sailing, rowing and  dragon boating are held on Canberra's lakes.<sup about="#mwt1290" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Top_ways_347-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Top ways"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Top_ways-347"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Top_ways-347" id="mwCiw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCi0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCi4">[</span>343<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCi8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-348" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-348"}}'><a href="#cite_note-348" id="mwCjA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjI">[</span>344<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjM">]</span></span></a></sup> A popular form of exercise for people working near or in the Parliamentary Triangle is to do the "bridge to bridge walk/run" of about 5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCjQ"> </span>km around <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Burley_Griffin" title="Lake Burley Griffin" id="mwCjU">Lake Burley Griffin</a>, crossing the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_Avenue_Bridge" title="Commonwealth Avenue Bridge" id="mwCjY">Commonwealth Avenue Bridge</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kings_Avenue,_Canberra" title="Kings Avenue, Canberra" id="mwCjc">Kings Avenue Bridge</a>, using the paths beside the lake. The walk takes about 1 hour, making it ideal for a lunchtime excursion. This is also popular on weekends. Such was the popularity during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19" title="COVID-19" id="mwCjg">COVID-19</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_coronavirus_pandemic_in_Australia#Australian_Capital_Territory" title="2020 coronavirus pandemic in Australia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCjk">isolation in 2020</a> that the ACT Government initiated a 'Clockwise is COVID-wise' rule for walkers and runners.<sup about="#mwt1294" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Top_ways_347-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Top ways"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Top_ways-347" id="mwCjo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjw">[</span>343<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCj0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1296" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2020-04-19_ABC_349-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"2020-04-19_ABC"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2020-04-19_ABC-349"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2020-04-19_ABC-349" id="mwCj4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCj8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkA">[</span>345<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

