</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwCsk" aria-labelledby="Infrastructure"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Infrastructure">Infrastructure</h2></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwCso" aria-labelledby="Health"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Health">Health</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCss"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Hospital_February_2018.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCsw"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_Hospital_February_2018.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Canberra_Hospital_February_2018.jpg/250px-Canberra_Hospital_February_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Canberra_Hospital_February_2018.jpg/500px-Canberra_Hospital_February_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4048" data-file-height="3036" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCs0"/></a><figcaption id="mwCs4">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Hospital" title="Canberra Hospital" id="mwCs8">Canberra Hospital</a></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwCtA">Canberra has two large public hospitals, the approximately 600-bed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Hospital" title="Canberra Hospital" id="mwCtE">Canberra Hospital</a>—formerly the Woden Valley Hospital—in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garran,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Garran, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCtI">Garran</a> and the 250-bed North Canberra Hospital in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Bruce, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCtM">Bruce</a>.<sup about="#mwt1326" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-359" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-359"}}'><a href="#cite_note-359" id="mwCtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCtU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtY">[</span>355<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1329" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Canberra_Clinical_School_360-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Canberra Clinical School"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Canberra_Clinical_School-360"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Canberra_Clinical_School-360" id="mwCtg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCtk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCto">[</span>356<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCts">]</span></span></a></sup> The latter was called Calvary Public Hospital Bruce before its acquisition by the ACT Government in 2023.<sup about="#mwt1332" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-361" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-361"}}'><a href="#cite_note-361" id="mwCtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCt0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCt4">[</span>357<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCt8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1335" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-362" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-362"}}'><a href="#cite_note-362" id="mwCuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuI">[</span>358<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuM">]</span></span></a></sup> Both are teaching institutions.<sup about="#mwt1336" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Canberra_Clinical_School_360-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Canberra Clinical School"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Canberra_Clinical_School-360" id="mwCuQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuY">[</span>356<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuc">]</span></span></a></sup> The largest private hospital is the Calvary John James Hospital in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deakin,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Deakin, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwCug">Deakin</a>, which is being redeveloped to include 98 beds by 2028,<sup about="#mwt1339" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-363" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-363"}}'><a href="#cite_note-363" id="mwCuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCus">[</span>359<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuw">]</span></span></a></sup> Calvary Bruce Private Hospital<sup about="#mwt1342" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-364" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-364"}}'><a href="#cite_note-364" id="mwCu0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCu4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCu8">[</span>360<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvA">]</span></span></a></sup> in Bruce and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Healthscope" title="Healthscope" id="mwCvE">Healthscope</a>'s National Capital Private Hospital <sup about="#mwt1345" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-365" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-365"}}'><a href="#cite_note-365" id="mwCvI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvQ">[</span>361<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvU">]</span></span></a></sup> in Garran are also major healthcare providers.</p>

<p id="mwCvY">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Canberra_Hospital" title="Royal Canberra Hospital" id="mwCvc">Royal Canberra Hospital</a> was located on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acton_Peninsula" title="Acton Peninsula" id="mwCvg">Acton Peninsula</a> on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Burley_Griffin" title="Lake Burley Griffin" id="mwCvk">Lake Burley Griffin</a>; it was closed in 1991 and was demolished in 1997 in a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Canberra_Hospital_implosion" title="Royal Canberra Hospital implosion" id="mwCvo">controversial and fatal implosion</a> to facilitate construction of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Museum_of_Australia" title="National Museum of Australia" id="mwCvs">National Museum of Australia</a>.<sup about="#mwt1346" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198818_105-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission198818"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198818-105"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"18"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198818-105" id="mwCvw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCv0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCv4">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCv8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1349" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817_167-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTENational Capital Development Commission198817"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"National Capital Development Commission"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"p":{"wt":"17"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTENational_Capital_Development_Commission198817-167" id="mwCwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwI">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1352" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-map_176-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"map"}}'><a href="#cite_note-map-176" id="mwCwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwY">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1355" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-366" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-366"}}'><a href="#cite_note-366" id="mwCwg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwo">[</span>362<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCws">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1358" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-367" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-367"}}'><a href="#cite_note-367" id="mwCww"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCw4">[</span>363<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCw8">]</span></span></a></sup>  Ambulance services are provided by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACT_Ambulance_Service" title="ACT Ambulance Service" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCxA">ACT Ambulance Service</a>, one of four operational agencies of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Capital_Territory_Emergency_Services_Agency" title="Australian Capital Territory Emergency Services Agency" id="mwCxE">ACT Emergency Services Agency</a>.<sup about="#mwt1361" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-368" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-368"}}'><a href="#cite_note-368" id="mwCxI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxQ">[</span>364<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="25" id="mwCxY" aria-labelledby="Transport"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Transport">Transport</h3></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="26" id="mwCxc" aria-labelledby="Roads"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Roads">Roads</h4></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCxg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Highways_into_Canberra_(6768361501).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCxk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Highways_into_Canberra_(6768361501).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Highways_into_Canberra_%286768361501%29.jpg/250px-Highways_into_Canberra_%286768361501%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Highways_into_Canberra_%286768361501%29.jpg/500px-Highways_into_Canberra_%286768361501%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4368" data-file-height="2912" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCxo"/></a><figcaption id="mwCxs">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenloch_Interchange" title="Glenloch Interchange" id="mwCxw">Glenloch Interchange</a> connects the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuggeranong_Parkway" title="Tuggeranong Parkway" id="mwCx0">Tuggeranong Parkway</a> with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkes_Way" title="Parkes Way" id="mwCx4">Parkes Way</a></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCx8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ACTION_(BUS_680)_Volgren_Optimus_bodied_Scania_K360UA_6x2-2_(Euro_VI)_at_the_intersection_of_Alinga_St_and_Northbourne_Ave_(1).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCyA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:ACTION_(BUS_680)_Volgren_Optimus_bodied_Scania_K360UA_6x2-2_(Euro_VI)_at_the_intersection_of_Alinga_St_and_Northbourne_Ave_(1).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/ACTION_%28BUS_680%29_Volgren_Optimus_bodied_Scania_K360UA_6x2-2_%28Euro_VI%29_at_the_intersection_of_Alinga_St_and_Northbourne_Ave_%281%29.jpg/250px-ACTION_%28BUS_680%29_Volgren_Optimus_bodied_Scania_K360UA_6x2-2_%28Euro_VI%29_at_the_intersection_of_Alinga_St_and_Northbourne_Ave_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/ACTION_%28BUS_680%29_Volgren_Optimus_bodied_Scania_K360UA_6x2-2_%28Euro_VI%29_at_the_intersection_of_Alinga_St_and_Northbourne_Ave_%281%29.jpg/500px-ACTION_%28BUS_680%29_Volgren_Optimus_bodied_Scania_K360UA_6x2-2_%28Euro_VI%29_at_the_intersection_of_Alinga_St_and_Northbourne_Ave_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCyE"/></a><figcaption id="mwCyI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACTION" title="ACTION" id="mwCyM">ACTION</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volgren" title="Volgren" id="mwCyQ">Volgren</a> bodied <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scania_K-series" title="Scania K-series" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCyU">Scania K360UA</a></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCyY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tram_at_Alinga_Street_light_rail_stop_July_2022.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCyc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tram_at_Alinga_Street_light_rail_stop_July_2022.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tram_at_Alinga_Street_light_rail_stop_July_2022.jpg/250px-Tram_at_Alinga_Street_light_rail_stop_July_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Tram_at_Alinga_Street_light_rail_stop_July_2022.jpg/500px-Tram_at_Alinga_Street_light_rail_stop_July_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCyg"/></a><figcaption id="mwCyk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alinga_Street_light_rail_station" title="Alinga Street light rail station" id="mwCyo">Alinga Street light rail station</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCys">The automobile is by far the dominant form of transport in Canberra, comprising 76.5% of trips in 2017.<sup about="#mwt1368" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-road_369-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"road"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-road-369"}}'><a href="#cite_note-road-369" id="mwCyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCy0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCy4">[</span>365<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCy8">]</span></span></a></sup> The speed limit in most suburban roads is <span about="#mwt1362" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"50"},"2":{"wt":"km/h"}},"i":0}}]}'>50</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1362"> </span><span about="#mwt1362">km/h (31</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1362"> </span><span about="#mwt1362">mph)</span>, but some major suburban roads have a speed limit of <span about="#mwt1363" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"60"},"2":{"wt":"km/h"}},"i":0}}]}'>60</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1363"> </span><span about="#mwt1363">km/h (37</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1363"> </span><span about="#mwt1363">mph)</span>. School zones, for some hours on school days, and town centres have limits of <span about="#mwt1364" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"40"},"2":{"wt":"km/h"}},"i":0}}]}'>40</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1364"> </span><span about="#mwt1364">km/h (25</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1364"> </span><span about="#mwt1364">mph)</span>.<sup about="#mwt1371" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-370" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-370"}}'><a href="#cite_note-370" id="mwCzM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzU">[</span>366<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzY">]</span></span></a></sup> Limited access <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dual_carriageway" title="Dual carriageway" id="mwCzc">dual carriageway</a> roads, generally known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkway" title="Parkway" id="mwCzg">parkways</a>, have higher speed limits, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuggeranong_Parkway" title="Tuggeranong Parkway" id="mwCzk">Tuggeranong Parkway</a>, which links Canberra's CBD and Tuggeranong and has a speed limit of <span about="#mwt1365" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCzo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cvt","href":"./Template:Cvt"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"100"},"2":{"wt":"km/h"}},"i":0}}]}'>100</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1365"> </span><span about="#mwt1365">km/h (62</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1365"> </span><span about="#mwt1365">mph)</span> for most of its length.<sup about="#mwt1374" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-371" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-371"}}'><a href="#cite_note-371" id="mwCzs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCz0">[</span>367<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCz4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCz8">In 1974 the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Capital_Authority#1958–1989:_National_Capital_Development_Commission_(NCDC)" title="National Capital Authority" id="mwC0A">National Capital Development Commission</a> announced a shift in transport planning to prioritise public transport and discourage commuting by car.<sup about="#mwt1377" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-372" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-372"}}'><a href="#cite_note-372" id="mwC0E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0M">[</span>368<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0Q">]</span></span></a></sup> The Commission's Transport Policy was a progressive, possibly radical, approach to transport planning for the time. Unwilling to accept the advice of a 1977 traffic study, the NCDC abandoned its commitment to expert-led planning, suppressed the modelling report and revived its car-oriented transport plans from the 1960s.<sup about="#mwt1380" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Mees2014_373-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Mees2014"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mees2014-373"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Mees2014-373" id="mwC0U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0c">[</span>369<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0g">]</span></span></a></sup> This led to Canberra being a car-dominated city today. In 2006 Canberrans were the most likely of any Australian city dwellers to use their cars to get to work.<sup about="#mwt1383" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-374" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-374"}}'><a href="#cite_note-374" id="mwC0k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0s">[</span>370<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC00">In an effort to improve road safety, traffic cameras were first introduced to Canberra by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Carnell" title="Kate Carnell" id="mwC04">Kate Carnell</a> Government in 1999.<sup about="#mwt1386" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-LawsonTraffic_375-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"LawsonTraffic"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-LawsonTraffic-375"}}'><a href="#cite_note-LawsonTraffic-375" id="mwC08"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1E">[</span>371<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1I">]</span></span></a></sup> The traffic cameras installed in Canberra include fixed red-light and speed cameras and point-to-point speed cameras; together they brought in revenue of approximately $11<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC1M"> </span>million per year in fines in about 2014.<sup about="#mwt1387" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-LawsonTraffic_375-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"LawsonTraffic"}}'><a href="#cite_note-LawsonTraffic-375" id="mwC1Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1Y">[</span>371<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1c">]</span></span></a></sup>
There are two local taxi companies. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aerial_Consolidated_Transport" title="Aerial Consolidated Transport" id="mwC1g">Aerial Capital Group</a> enjoyed monopoly status until the arrival of Cabxpress in 2007.<sup about="#mwt1390" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-376" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-376"}}'><a href="#cite_note-376" id="mwC1k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1s">[</span>372<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1w">]</span></span></a></sup> In October 2015 the ACT Government passed legislation to regulate ride sharing, allowing ride share services including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uber" title="Uber" id="mwC10">Uber</a> to operate legally in Canberra.<sup about="#mwt1393" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-377" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-377"}}'><a href="#cite_note-377" id="mwC14"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC18"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2A">[</span>373<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1396" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-378" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-378"}}'><a href="#cite_note-378" id="mwC2I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2Q">[</span>374<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2U">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1399" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-379" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-379"}}'><a href="#cite_note-379" id="mwC2Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2g">[</span>375<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2k">]</span></span></a></sup> The ACT Government was the first jurisdiction in Australia to enact legislation to regulate the service.<sup about="#mwt1402" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-380" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-380"}}'><a href="#cite_note-380" id="mwC2o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2w">[</span>376<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC20">]</span></span></a></sup> Since then many other ride sharing and taxi services have started in ACT namely <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ola_Cabs" title="Ola Cabs" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC24">Ola</a>, Glide Taxi<sup about="#mwt1405" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-381" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-381"}}'><a href="#cite_note-381" id="mwC28"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3E">[</span>377<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3I">]</span></span></a></sup> and GoCatch<sup about="#mwt1408" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-382" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-382"}}'><a href="#cite_note-382" id="mwC3M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3U">[</span>378<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC3c">Canberra is about three hours by road from Sydney on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Highway_(Australia)" title="Federal Highway (Australia)" id="mwC3g">Federal Highway</a> (National Highway 23),<sup about="#mwt1409" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia2000inside_cover_383-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPenguin Books Australia2000inside cover"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia2000inside_cover-383"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Penguin Books Australia"},"2":{"wt":"2000"},"loc":{"wt":"inside cover"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia2000inside_cover-383" id="mwC3k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3s">[</span>379<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3w">]</span></span></a></sup> which connects with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hume_Highway" title="Hume Highway" id="mwC30">Hume Highway</a> (National Highway 31) near <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goulburn" title="Goulburn" id="mwC34">Goulburn</a>, and seven hours by road from Melbourne on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barton_Highway" title="Barton Highway" id="mwC38">Barton Highway</a> (National Highway 25), which joins the Hume Highway at Yass.<sup about="#mwt1412" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia2000inside_cover_383-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPenguin Books Australia2000inside cover"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia2000inside_cover-383"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Penguin Books Australia"},"2":{"wt":"2000"},"loc":{"wt":"inside cover"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia2000inside_cover-383" id="mwC4A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4I">[</span>379<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4M">]</span></span></a></sup> It is a two-hour drive on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monaro_Highway" title="Monaro Highway" id="mwC4Q">Monaro Highway</a> (National Highway 23) to the ski fields of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowy_Mountains" title="Snowy Mountains" id="mwC4U">Snowy Mountains</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kosciuszko_National_Park" title="Kosciuszko National Park" id="mwC4Y">Kosciuszko National Park</a>.<sup about="#mwt1415" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020_384-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPenguin Books Australia200020"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020-384"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Penguin Books Australia"},"2":{"wt":"2000"},"p":{"wt":"20"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020-384" id="mwC4c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4k">[</span>380<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4o">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batemans_Bay" title="Batemans Bay" id="mwC4s">Batemans Bay</a>, a popular holiday spot on the New South Wales coast, is also two hours away via the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kings_Highway,_Australia" title="Kings Highway, Australia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC4w">Kings Highway</a>.<sup about="#mwt1418" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020_384-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPenguin Books Australia200020"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020-384"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Penguin Books Australia"},"2":{"wt":"2000"},"p":{"wt":"20"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020-384" id="mwC40"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC44"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC48">[</span>380<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5A">]</span></span></a></sup> Interstate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coach_(bus)" title="Coach (bus)" id="mwC5E">coach</a> services operate on these roads, with three companies operating a Sydney-Canberra express route: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murrays" title="Murrays" id="mwC5I">Murrays</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FlixBus" title="FlixBus" id="mwC5M">FlixBus</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greyhound_Australia" title="Greyhound Australia" id="mwC5Q">Greyhound Australia</a>.<sup about="#mwt1423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-385" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-385"}}'><a href="#cite_note-385" id="mwC5U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5c">[</span>381<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5g">]</span></span></a></sup> Other coach routes include: Murrays buses to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wollongong" title="Wollongong" id="mwC5k">Wollongong</a> (via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss_Vale" title="Moss Vale" id="mwC5o">Moss Vale</a>) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narooma" title="Narooma" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC5s">Narooma</a> (via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batemans_Bay" title="Batemans Bay" id="mwC5w">Batemans Bay</a>); FlixBus buses to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melbourne" title="Melbourne" id="mwC50">Melbourne</a> (via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albury,_New_South_Wales" title="Albury, New South Wales" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC54">Albury</a>); <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V/Line" title="V/Line" id="mwC58">V/Line</a> buses to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wodonga" title="Wodonga" id="mwC6A">Wodonga</a> (via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gundagai" title="Gundagai" id="mwC6E">Gundagai</a>) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bairnsdale,_Victoria" title="Bairnsdale, Victoria" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC6I">Bairnsdale</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traralgon" title="Traralgon" id="mwC6M">Traralgon</a> (via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooma" title="Cooma" id="mwC6Q">Cooma</a>); <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSW_TrainLink" title="NSW TrainLink" id="mwC6U">NSW TrainLink</a> buses to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombala,_New_South_Wales" title="Bombala, New South Wales" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC6Y">Bombala</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eden,_New_South_Wales" title="Eden, New South Wales" id="mwC6c">Eden</a> (via Cooma), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagga_Wagga" title="Wagga Wagga" id="mwC6g">Wagga Wagga</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cootamundra" title="Cootamundra" id="mwC6k">Cootamundra</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goulburn,_New_South_Wales" title="Goulburn, New South Wales" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC6o">Goulburn</a>; and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CDC_Canberra" title="CDC Canberra" id="mwC6s">CDC Canberra</a> buses to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queanbeyan" title="Queanbeyan" id="mwC6w">Queanbeyan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yass,_New_South_Wales" title="Yass, New South Wales" id="mwC60">Yass</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bungendore" title="Bungendore" id="mwC64">Bungendore</a>.<sup about="#mwt1426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-386" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-386"}}'><a href="#cite_note-386" id="mwC68"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7E">[</span>382<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7I">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="27" id="mwC7M" aria-labelledby="Public_transport"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Public_transport">Public transport</h4></div>
<p id="mwC7Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transport_Canberra_&amp;_City_Services" title="Transport Canberra &amp; City Services" id="mwC7U">Transport Canberra</a> provides bus and light rail services throughout the city.<sup about="#mwt1429" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-387" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-387"}}'><a href="#cite_note-387" id="mwC7Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7g">[</span>383<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7k">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CDC_Canberra" title="CDC Canberra" id="mwC7o">CDC Canberra</a> provides bus services between Canberra and nearby areas of New South Wales, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queanbeyan" title="Queanbeyan" id="mwC7s">Queanbeyan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bungendore" title="Bungendore" id="mwC7w">Bungendore</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murrumbateman" title="Murrumbateman" id="mwC70">Murrumbateman</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yass,_New_South_Wales" title="Yass, New South Wales" id="mwC74">Yass</a>.<sup about="#mwt1432" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-388" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-388"}}'><a href="#cite_note-388" id="mwC78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8E">[</span>384<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8I">]</span></span></a></sup> A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light_rail_in_Canberra" title="Light rail in Canberra" id="mwC8M">light rail line</a> commenced service on 20 April 2019 linking the CBD with the northern district of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gungahlin" title="Gungahlin" id="mwC8Q">Gungahlin</a>.<sup about="#mwt1435" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-389" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-389"}}'><a href="#cite_note-389" id="mwC8U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8c">[</span>385<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8g">]</span></span></a></sup> A planned Stage 2A of Canberra's light rail network will run from Alinga Street station to Commonwealth Park, adding three new stops at City West, City South and Commonwealth Park.<sup about="#mwt1438" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-390" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-390"}}'><a href="#cite_note-390" id="mwC8k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8s">[</span>386<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8w">]</span></span></a></sup> Work on stage 2 commenced in November 2022<sup about="#mwt1441" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-391" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-391"}}'><a href="#cite_note-391" id="mwC80"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC84"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC88">[</span>387<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9A">]</span></span></a></sup> and the line is expected to be open in early 2028.<sup about="#mwt1444" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-392" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-392"}}'><a href="#cite_note-392" id="mwC9E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC9I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9M">[</span>388<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9Q">]</span></span></a></sup> At the 2021 census, 6.3% of the journeys to work involved public transport, while 4.0% walked to work.<sup about="#mwt1445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Census2021_201-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Census2021"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Census2021-201" id="mwC9U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC9Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9c">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="28" id="mwC9k" aria-labelledby="Interstate_rail"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Interstate_rail">Interstate rail</h4></div>

<p id="mwC9o">An interstate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NSW_TrainLink" title="NSW TrainLink" id="mwC9s">NSW TrainLink</a> railway service connects Canberra to Sydney.<sup about="#mwt1452" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-traindestinations_393-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"traindestinations"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-traindestinations-393"}}'><a href="#cite_note-traindestinations-393" id="mwC9w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC90"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC94">[</span>389<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC98">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_railway_station" title="Canberra railway station" id="mwC-A">Canberra railway station</a> is in the inner south suburb of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingston,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Kingston, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwC-E">Kingston</a>.<sup about="#mwt1455" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-394" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-394"}}'><a href="#cite_note-394" id="mwC-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-Q">[</span>390<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-U">]</span></span></a></sup> Between 1920 and 1922 the train line crossed the Molonglo River and ran as far north as the city centre, although the line was closed following major flooding and was never rebuilt, while plans for a line to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yass,_New_South_Wales" title="Yass, New South Wales" id="mwC-Y">Yass</a> were abandoned. A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3_ft_6_in_gauge_railways" title="3 ft 6 in gauge railways" about="#mwt1446" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC-c" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"RailGauge","href":"./Template:RailGauge"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"3ft6in"},"lk":{"wt":"on"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="nowrap">3<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>ft<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>6<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>in</span></a><span about="#mwt1446"> (</span><span class="nowrap" about="#mwt1446">1,067<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>mm</span><span about="#mwt1446">)</span> gauge construction railway was built in 1923 between the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yarralumla_brickworks" title="Yarralumla brickworks" id="mwC-g">Yarralumla brickworks</a> and the provisional Parliament House; it was later extended to Civic, but the whole line was closed in May 1927.<sup about="#mwt1458" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-395" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-395"}}'><a href="#cite_note-395" id="mwC-k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-s">[</span>391<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-w">]</span></span></a></sup> Train services to Melbourne are provided by way of a NSW TrainLink bus service which connects with a rail service between Sydney and Melbourne in Yass, about a one-hour drive from Canberra.<sup about="#mwt1459" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-traindestinations_393-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"traindestinations"}}'><a href="#cite_note-traindestinations-393" id="mwC-0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-8">[</span>389<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1447" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020_384-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEPenguin Books Australia200020"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020-384"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Penguin Books Australia"},"2":{"wt":"2000"},"p":{"wt":"20"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPenguin_Books_Australia200020-384" id="mwC_E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_M">[</span>380<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC_U">Plans to establish a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High-speed_rail_in_Australia" title="High-speed rail in Australia" id="mwC_Y">high-speed rail</a> service between Melbourne, Canberra and Sydney,<sup about="#mwt1465" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-396" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-396"}}'><a href="#cite_note-396" id="mwC_c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_k">[</span>392<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_o">]</span></span></a></sup> have not been implemented, as the various proposals have been deemed economically unviable.<sup about="#mwt1468" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-397" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-397"}}'><a href="#cite_note-397" id="mwC_s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_0">[</span>393<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1471" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-398" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-398"}}'><a href="#cite_note-398" id="mwC_8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAE">[</span>394<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAI">]</span></span></a></sup> The original plans for Canberra included proposals for railed transport within the city,<sup about="#mwt1474" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-railways_399-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"railways"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-railways-399"}}'><a href="#cite_note-railways-399" id="mwDAM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAU">[</span>395<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAY">]</span></span></a></sup> however none eventuated.<sup about="#mwt1475" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-railways_399-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"railways"}}'><a href="#cite_note-railways-399" id="mwDAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAk">[</span>395<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAo">]</span></span></a></sup> The phase 2 report of the most recent proposal, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High-speed_rail_in_Australia#High-Speed_Rail_Study_(2008–2013)" title="High-speed rail in Australia" id="mwDAs">High Speed Rail Study</a>, was published by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Infrastructure_and_Transport" title="Department of Infrastructure and Transport" id="mwDAw">Department of Infrastructure and Transport</a> on 11 April 2013.<sup about="#mwt1478" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-400" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-400"}}'><a href="#cite_note-400" id="mwDA0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDA4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA8">[</span>396<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBA">]</span></span></a></sup> A railway connecting Canberra to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jervis_Bay" title="Jervis Bay" id="mwDBE">Jervis Bay</a> was also planned but never constructed.<sup about="#mwt1460" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGibbney198858,_60_401-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGibbney198858, 60"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGibbney198858,_60-401"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Gibbney"},"2":{"wt":"1988"},"pp":{"wt":"58, 60"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGibbney198858,_60-401" id="mwDBI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDBM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBQ">[</span>397<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDBY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_International_Airport_01.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDBc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Canberra_International_Airport_01.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Canberra_International_Airport_01.jpg/250px-Canberra_International_Airport_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Canberra_International_Airport_01.jpg/500px-Canberra_International_Airport_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDBg"/></a><figcaption id="mwDBk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Airport" title="Canberra Airport" id="mwDBo">Canberra Airport</a> terminal</figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="29" id="mwDBs" aria-labelledby="Air_travel"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Air_travel">Air travel</h4></div>
<p id="mwDBw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Airport" title="Canberra Airport" id="mwDB0">Canberra Airport</a> provides direct domestic services to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide_Airport" title="Adelaide Airport" id="mwDB4">Adelaide</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brisbane_Airport" title="Brisbane Airport" id="mwDB8">Brisbane</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cairns_Airport" title="Cairns Airport" id="mwDCA">Cairns</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darwin_Airport" title="Darwin Airport" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDCE">Darwin</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_Coast_Airport" title="Gold Coast Airport" id="mwDCI">Gold Coast</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hobart_Airport" title="Hobart Airport" id="mwDCM">Hobart</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melbourne_Airport" title="Melbourne Airport" id="mwDCQ">Melbourne</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perth_Airport" title="Perth Airport" id="mwDCU">Perth</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunshine_Coast_Airport" title="Sunshine Coast Airport" id="mwDCY">Sunshine Coast</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sydney_Airport" title="Sydney Airport" id="mwDCc">Sydney</a> with connections to other domestic centres.<sup about="#mwt1481" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-402" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-402"}}'><a href="#cite_note-402" id="mwDCg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDCk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCo">[</span>398<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCs">]</span></span></a></sup> There are also direct flights to small regional towns: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballina_Byron_Gateway_Airport" title="Ballina Byron Gateway Airport" id="mwDCw">Ballina</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dubbo_Regional_Airport" title="Dubbo Regional Airport" id="mwDC0">Dubbo</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newcastle_Airport,_New_South_Wales" title="Newcastle Airport, New South Wales" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDC4">Newcastle</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Macquarie_Airport" title="Port Macquarie Airport" id="mwDC8">Port Macquarie</a> in New South Wales. Canberra Airport is, as of September 2013, designated by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Infrastructure_and_Regional_Development" title="Department of Infrastructure and Regional Development" id="mwDDA">Australian Government Department of Infrastructure and Regional Development</a> as a restricted use designated international airport.<sup about="#mwt1484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-403" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-403"}}'><a href="#cite_note-403" id="mwDDE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDDI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDM">[</span>399<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDQ">]</span></span></a></sup> International flights have previously been operated by both <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore_Airlines" title="Singapore Airlines" id="mwDDU">Singapore Airlines</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qatar_Airways" title="Qatar Airways" id="mwDDY">Qatar Airways</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiji_Airways" title="Fiji Airways" id="mwDDc">Fiji Airways</a> has announced direct flights to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nadi" title="Nadi" id="mwDDg">Nadi</a> commencing in July 2023.<sup about="#mwt1487" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-404" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-404"}}'><a href="#cite_note-404" id="mwDDk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDDo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDs">[</span>400<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDw">]</span></span></a></sup> Until 2003 the civilian airport shared runways with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairbairn_airbase" title="Fairbairn airbase" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDD0">RAAF Base Fairbairn</a>. In June of that year, the Air Force base was decommissioned and from that time the airport was fully under civilian control.<sup about="#mwt1490" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-405" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-405"}}'><a href="#cite_note-405" id="mwDD4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDD8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEA">[</span>401<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="30" id="mwDEI" aria-labelledby="Active_transport"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Active_transport">Active transport</h4></div>

<p id="mwDEM">Canberra has one of the highest rates of active travel of all Australian major cities, with 7.1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDEQ"> </span>per<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDEU"> </span>cent of commuters walking or cycling to work in 2011.<sup about="#mwt1493" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-406" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-406"}}'><a href="#cite_note-406" id="mwDEY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEg">[</span>402<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEk">]</span></span></a></sup> An ACT Government survey conducted in late 2010 found that Canberrans walk an average of 26<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDEo"> </span>minutes each day.<sup about="#mwt1496" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-407" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-407"}}'><a href="#cite_note-407" id="mwDEs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDE0">[</span>403<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDE4">]</span></span></a></sup> According to <i id="mwDE8">The Canberra Times</i> in March 2014, Canberra's cyclists are involved in an average of four reported collisions every week.<sup about="#mwt1499" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-408" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-408"}}'><a href="#cite_note-408" id="mwDFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFI">[</span>404<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFM">]</span></span></a></sup> The newspaper also reported that Canberra is home to 87,000 cyclists, translating to the highest cycling participation rate in Australia; and, with higher popularity, bike injury rates in 2012 were twice the national average.<sup about="#mwt1502" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-409" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-409"}}'><a href="#cite_note-409" id="mwDFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFY">[</span>405<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDFg">Since late 2020, two <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scooter-sharing_system" title="Scooter-sharing system" id="mwDFk">scooter-sharing systems</a> have been operational in Canberra: orange scooters from Neuron Mobility and purple scooters from Beam Mobility,<sup about="#mwt1505" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-410" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-410"}}'><a href="#cite_note-410" id="mwDFo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFw">[</span>406<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDF0">]</span></span></a></sup> both <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore" title="Singapore" id="mwDF4">Singapore</a>-based companies that operate in many Australian cities. These services cover much of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra_Central" title="Canberra Central" id="mwDF8">Canberra Central</a> and Central <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belconnen" title="Belconnen" id="mwDGA">Belconnen</a>, with plans to expand coverage to more areas of the city in 2022.<sup about="#mwt1508" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-411" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-411"}}'><a href="#cite_note-411" id="mwDGE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGM">[</span>407<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="31" id="mwDGU" aria-labelledby="Utilities"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Utilities">Utilities</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDGY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm_August_2024.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDGc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm_August_2024.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm_August_2024.jpg/250px-Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm_August_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm_August_2024.jpg/500px-Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm_August_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4032" data-file-height="3024" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDGg"/></a><figcaption id="mwDGk">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm" title="Mount Majura Solar Farm" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDGo">Mount Majura Solar Farm</a> has a rated output of 2.3 megawatts and was opened on 6 October 2016.<sup about="#mwt1511" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Solar_Choice_412-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Solar Choice"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Solar_Choice-412"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Solar_Choice-412" id="mwDGs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDG0">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDG4">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwDG8">The government-owned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icon_Water" title="Icon Water" id="mwDHA">Icon Water</a> manages Canberra's water and sewerage infrastructure.<sup about="#mwt1514" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-413" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-413"}}'><a href="#cite_note-413" id="mwDHE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDHI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHM">[</span>409<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ActewAGL" title="ActewAGL" id="mwDHU">ActewAGL</a> is a joint venture between ACTEW and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Gas_Light_Company" title="Australian Gas Light Company" id="mwDHY">AGL</a>, and is the retail provider of Canberra's utility services including water, natural gas, electricity, and also some telecommunications services via a subsidiary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TransACT" title="TransACT" id="mwDHc">TransACT</a>.<sup about="#mwt1517" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-414" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-414"}}'><a href="#cite_note-414" id="mwDHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDHk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHo">[</span>410<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDHw">Canberra's water is stored in four reservoirs, the Corin, Bendora and Cotter dams on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotter_River" title="Cotter River" id="mwDH0">Cotter River</a> and the Googong Dam on the Queanbeyan River. Although the Googong Dam is located in New South Wales, it is managed by the ACT government.<sup about="#mwt1520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-415" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-415"}}'><a href="#cite_note-415" id="mwDH4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDH8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIA">[</span>411<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIE">]</span></span></a></sup> Icon Water owns Canberra's two wastewater treatment plants, located at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyshwick" title="Fyshwick" id="mwDII">Fyshwick</a> and on the lower reaches of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molonglo_River" title="Molonglo River" id="mwDIM">Molonglo River</a>.<sup about="#mwt1523" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-416" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-416"}}'><a href="#cite_note-416" id="mwDIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIY">[</span>412<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1526" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-417" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-417"}}'><a href="#cite_note-417" id="mwDIg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIo">[</span>413<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDIw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy_in_the_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Energy in the Australian Capital Territory" id="mwDI0">Electricity for Canberra</a> mainly comes from the national power grid through substations at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holt,_Australian_Capital_Territory" title="Holt, Australian Capital Territory" id="mwDI4">Holt</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyshwick" title="Fyshwick" id="mwDI8">Fyshwick</a> (via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queanbeyan" title="Queanbeyan" id="mwDJA">Queanbeyan</a>).<sup about="#mwt1529" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-418" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-418"}}'><a href="#cite_note-418" id="mwDJE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJM">[</span>414<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Power was first supplied from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingston_Powerhouse" title="Kingston Powerhouse" id="mwDJU">Kingston Powerhouse</a> near the Molonglo River, a thermal plant built in 1913, but this was finally closed in 1957.<sup about="#mwt1532" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-419" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-419"}}'><a href="#cite_note-419" id="mwDJY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJg">[</span>415<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-420" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-420"}}'><a href="#cite_note-420" id="mwDJo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJw">[</span>416<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJ0">]</span></span></a></sup> The ACT has four solar farms, which were opened between 2014 and 2017: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royalla_Solar_Farm" title="Royalla Solar Farm" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDJ4">Royalla</a> (rated output of 20 megawatts, 2014),<sup about="#mwt1538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-421" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-421"}}'><a href="#cite_note-421" id="mwDJ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKE">[</span>417<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKI">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Majura_Solar_Farm" title="Mount Majura Solar Farm" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDKM">Mount Majura</a> (2.3 MW, 2016),<sup about="#mwt1539" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Solar_Choice_412-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Solar Choice"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Solar_Choice-412" id="mwDKQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKY">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKc">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mugga_Lane_Solar_Park" title="Mugga Lane Solar Park" id="mwDKg">Mugga Lane</a> (13 MW, 2017)<sup about="#mwt1542" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-422" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-422"}}'><a href="#cite_note-422" id="mwDKk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKs">[</span>418<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKw">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamsdale_Solar_Farm" title="Williamsdale Solar Farm" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDK0">Williamsdale</a> (11 MW, 2017).<sup about="#mwt1545" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-423" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-423"}}'><a href="#cite_note-423" id="mwDK4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDK8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLA">[</span>419<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLE">]</span></span></a></sup> In addition, numerous houses in Canberra have photovoltaic panels or solar hot water systems. In 2015 and 2016, rooftop solar systems supported by the ACT government's feed-in tariff had a capacity of 26.3 megawatts, producing 34,910 MWh. In the same year, retailer-supported schemes had a capacity of 25.2 megawatts and exported 28,815 MWh to the grid (power consumed locally was not recorded).<sup about="#mwt1548" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-424" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-424"}}'><a href="#cite_note-424" id="mwDLI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLQ">[</span>420<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDLY">There are no wind-power generators in Canberra, but several have been built or are being built or planned in nearby New South Wales, such as the 140.7 megawatt <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_Wind_Farm" title="Capital Wind Farm" id="mwDLc">Capital Wind Farm</a>. The ACT government announced in 2013 that it was raising the target for electricity consumed in the ACT to be supplied from renewable sources to 90% by 2020,<sup about="#mwt1551" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-renewable_187-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"renewable"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-renewable-187"}}'><a href="#cite_note-renewable-187" id="mwDLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLo">[</span>187<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLs">]</span></span></a></sup> raising the target from 210 to 550 megawatts.<sup about="#mwt1554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-425" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-425"}}'><a href="#cite_note-425" id="mwDLw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDL0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDL4">[</span>421<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDL8">]</span></span></a></sup> It announced in February 2015 that three wind farms in Victoria and South Australia would supply 200 megawatts of capacity; these are expected to be operational by 2017.<sup about="#mwt1557" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-426" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-426"}}'><a href="#cite_note-426" id="mwDMA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDME"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMI">[</span>422<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMM">]</span></span></a></sup> Contracts for the purchase of an additional 200 megawatts of power from two wind farms in South Australia and New South Wales were announced in December 2015 and March 2016.<sup about="#mwt1560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-427" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-427"}}'><a href="#cite_note-427" id="mwDMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMY">[</span>423<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-428" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-428"}}'><a href="#cite_note-428" id="mwDMg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMo">[</span>424<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMs">]</span></span></a></sup> The ACT government announced in 2014 that up to 23 megawatts of feed-in-tariff entitlements would be made available for the establishment of a facility in the ACT or surrounding region for burning household and business waste to produce electricity by 2020.<sup about="#mwt1566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-429" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-429"}}'><a href="#cite_note-429" id="mwDMw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDM0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDM4">[</span>425<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDM8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="32" id="mwDNA" aria-labelledby="Twin_towns_and_sister_cities"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Twin_towns_and_sister_cities">Twin towns and sister cities</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1567" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDNE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"List of twin towns and sister cities in Australia"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1568" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1567" id="mwDNI">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_twin_towns_and_sister_cities_in_Australia" title="List of twin towns and sister cities in Australia">List of twin towns and sister cities in Australia</a></div>
<p id="mwDNM">Canberra has three <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sister_city" title="Sister city" id="mwDNQ">sister cities</a>:</p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDNU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Toku_by_Shinki_Kato.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDNY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Toku_by_Shinki_Kato.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Toku_by_Shinki_Kato.jpg/250px-Toku_by_Shinki_Kato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Toku_by_Shinki_Kato.jpg/500px-Toku_by_Shinki_Kato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="4000" data-file-height="2252" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDNc"/></a><figcaption id="mwDNg"><i id="mwDNk">Toku</i> in the Canberra-Nara Peace Park, which is located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lennox_Gardens" title="Lennox Gardens" id="mwDNo">Lennox Gardens</a></figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwDNs"><li id="mwDNw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing" title="Beijing" id="mwDN0">Beijing</a>, China<sup about="#mwt1571" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Canberra_430-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Canberra"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Canberra-430"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Canberra-430" id="mwDN4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDN8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOA">[</span>426<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDOI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nara,_Nara" title="Nara, Nara" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDOM">Nara</a>, Japan<sup about="#mwt1572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Canberra_430-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Canberra"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Canberra-430" id="mwDOQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDOU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOY">[</span>426<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDOg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wellington" title="Wellington" id="mwDOk">Wellington</a>, New Zealand<sup about="#mwt1575" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-431" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-431"}}'><a href="#cite_note-431" id="mwDOo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDOs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOw">[</span>427<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDO0">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwDO4">In addition, Canberra has the following friendship cities:</p>

<ul id="mwDO8"><li id="mwDPA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hangzhou" title="Hangzhou" id="mwDPE">Hangzhou</a>, China: The ACT Government signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Hangzhou Municipal People's Government on 29 October 1998. The Agreement was designed to promote business opportunities and cultural exchanges between the two cities.<sup about="#mwt1578" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-432" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-432"}}'><a href="#cite_note-432" id="mwDPI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPQ">[</span>428<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDPY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dili" title="Dili" id="mwDPc">Dili</a>, East Timor: The Canberra Dili Friendship Agreement was signed in 2004, aiming to build friendship and mutual respect and promote educational, cultural, economic, humanitarian and sporting links between Canberra and Dili.<sup about="#mwt1581" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-433" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-433"}}'><a href="#cite_note-433" id="mwDPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPo">[</span>429<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDPw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nusantara" title="Nusantara" id="mwDP0">Nusantara</a>, Indonesia: Australia's National Capital Authority and Indonesia's Nusantara Capital City Authority signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on cooperation. Nusantara and Canberra are both designed and planned national capitals, making the MoU particularly unique and relevant. The MoU covers potential exchanges of people and information, joint studies and exhibitions, and other cooperation. It extends on support that the Australian Government has already provided towards the development of Nusantara.<sup about="#mwt1585" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-434" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-434"}}'><a href="#cite_note-434" id="mwDP4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDP8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQA">[</span>430<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQE">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<p id="mwDQI">City-to-city relationships encourage communities and special interest groups both locally and abroad to engage in a wide range of exchange activities. The Canberra Nara Candle Festival held annually in spring, is a community celebration of the Canberra Nara Sister City relationship.<sup about="#mwt1588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-435" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-435"}}'><a href="#cite_note-435" id="mwDQM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQU">[</span>431<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQY">]</span></span></a></sup> The festival is held in Canberra Nara Park on the shores of Lake Burley Griffin.<sup about="#mwt1592" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-436" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-436"}}'><a href="#cite_note-436" id="mwDQc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQk">[</span>432<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="33" id="mwDQs" aria-labelledby="See_also"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="See_also">See also</h2></div>
<style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1373117785" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1593" id="mwDQw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Portal/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Portal","href":"./Template:Portal"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Australia"}},"i":0}}]}'>.mw-parser-output .portalbox{padding:0;margin:0.5em 0;display:table;box-sizing:border-box;max-width:175px;list-style:none}.mw-parser-output .portalborder{border:1px solid var(--border-color-base,#a2a9b1);padding:0.1em;background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle,#f8f9fa)}.mw-parser-output .portalbox-entry{display:table-row;font-size:85%;line-height:110%;height:1.9em;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold}.mw-parser-output .portalbox-image{display:table-cell;padding:0.2em;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center}.mw-parser-output .portalbox-link{display:table-cell;padding:0.2em 0.2em 0.2em 0.3em;vertical-align:middle}@media(min-width:640px){.mw-parser-output .portalleft{margin:0.5em 1em 0.5em 0}.mw-parser-output .portalright{clear:right;float:right;margin:0.5em 0 0.5em 1em}}</style><ul role="navigation" aria-label="Portals" class="noprint portalbox portalborder portalright" about="#mwt1593" id="mwDQ0">
